<%!-- Hidden JS-hook anchors. When embedded inside a parent surface
     (e.g. MeetingLive), the parent already mounts these hooks; mounting
     them a second time would create duplicate elements with the same id
     (LiveKit Room would double-subscribe). Suppress them in embedded
     mode and let the parent own the singletons. --%>

<%!-- `#push-subscribe` used to be the first anchor here. It moved to
     `shell.html.heex` in task 019ffb7b stage 3, where it is a singleton
     covering every surface rather than only `/chat`, so the
     `:if={!@embedded}` guard it carried is gone too — a shell-level
     element cannot collide with itself. `@push_permission` is seeded and
     maintained by `PlatformWeb.ShellLive` and still drives
     `<.notification_banner>` below. --%>

<%!-- data-camera-enabled / data-mic-enabled carry the server's committed
     media intent. On a LiveKit reconnect (task 019e4b3e stage 3) the JS
     hook reads these off the dataset to re-engage the camera/mic WITHOUT
     waiting for a fresh LV push — reconnect-safe (Rowan's exact error was
     "unable to push hook event. LiveView not connected"). --%>
<div
  :if={!@embedded}
  id="meeting-client"
  phx-hook="MeetingClient"
  class="hidden"
  data-camera-enabled={to_string(@camera_enabled)}
  data-mic-enabled={to_string(@mic_enabled)}
>
</div>
<div :if={!@embedded} id="meeting-room" phx-hook="MeetingRoom" class="hidden"></div>
<div :if={!@embedded} id="meeting-soundboard" phx-hook="MeetingSoundboard" class="hidden"></div>

<.notification_banner
  :if={!@embedded}
  push_permission={@push_permission}
  dismissed={@notification_banner_dismissed}
/>

<%!-- Chat root must claim the full height of <main> AND set min-h-0 so its
     descendant flex columns (chat-drop-zone, #message-list) can correctly
     shrink-to-fit. Without min-h-0, the default `min-height: auto` on flex
     items lets long message lists push past the viewport — on iOS Safari /
     PWA standalone, this manifests as the bottom-tab nav being pushed
     below the visible area while messages scroll the document itself.
     PR #333 rooted the shell chrome but the chat surface was still
     blowing the layout from the inside. --%>
<div class="flex h-full min-h-0 overflow-hidden">
  <%!-- Desktop sidebar — sectioned channel rail (chat plan v2 Stage 2).

       The `hidden lg:flex` responsive gate keeps this whole rail invisible
       on mobile; the mobile flat-list path lives in the `mobile_browser_open`
       overlay below and is intentionally untouched. Same pattern as the
       icon-rail / bottom-rail split in shell.html.heex.

       Section order:
         1. Pinned   (renders only when non-empty; locked at top)
         2. DMs      (always shown; renders empty-state when no DMs)
         3. Sub-orgs (Paragon / Soylent / Fabrikam / Wayne-Tech / SXI, ALWAYS
                      rendered as section headers — empty buckets get an
                      empty-state hint instead of being suppressed)

       Stage 3 will wire drag-and-drop on the `.channel-section-drag-handle`
       affordance; today it's a static `☰` glyph that fades in on hover. --%>
  <%!-- rbac-external-users M5: the chrome-less external space rail. When
       `@external?` (M4 merges `chat_mode: "external"` into the connect session
       on the `chat.` host), ChatLive renders THIS branch INSTEAD of the internal
       discovery rail below — a single flat allowlisted-space list with NO sub-org
       section headers, NO pinned-task / archived sections, and NO new-channel /
       scope-pill / edit-layout / admin chrome (each of which leaks the internal
       workspace org tree). M4's `:external` app layout is chrome-less, so the Fabrikam
       branding + identity chip + logout that the icon-rail normally carries are
       rendered here at the rail head. Two paths, one ChatLive — mirrors the
       shipped `meet.` guest branch. Semantic DaisyUI tokens only (Fabrikam cyan
       primary is themed in app.css); mobile-first single column with
       env(safe-area-inset-*) padding. --%>
  <%!-- `hidden lg:flex` (task 019f9257-a83e): the external rail is desktop-only,
       mirroring the internal `#chat-sidebar` gate just below. On mobile it
       collapses entirely so the conversation pane spans the full viewport; the
       mobile substitute is the pills strip + `#external-mobile-switcher`
       overlay further down (both `lg:hidden`). --%>
  <aside
    :if={@external?}
    id="chat-external-rail"
    data-role="external-rail"
    class="hidden lg:flex w-72 max-w-[80vw] flex-shrink-0 flex-col border-r border-base-300 bg-base-200 lg:w-64"
  >
    <header
      class="flex-shrink-0 border-b border-base-300"
      style="padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top); padding-left: env(safe-area-inset-left);"
      data-role="external-rail-header"
    >
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-2.5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0" data-role="brand-chip">
          <img src={~p"/images/logo.svg"} alt="Fabrikam" class="size-6 flex-shrink-0" />
          <span class="truncate text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-base-content">
            Fabrikam
          </span>
        </div>
        <a
          href={~p"/auth/logout"}
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm btn-square"
          aria-label="Log out"
          data-role="external-logout"
        >
          <span class="hero-arrow-right-start-on-rectangle size-5"></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <%!-- Identity chip: who the external user is signed in as. Avatar + name
           only — NO org label (that would leak internal structure per canvas
           §7). --%>
      <div
        :if={@external_user}
        class="flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-base-300 px-3 py-2"
        data-role="external-identity"
      >
        <.human_avatar
          name={@external_user.name || @external_user.email || "You"}
          avatar_url={@external_user.avatar_url}
          seed={@external_user.oidc_sub || @external_user.email || @external_user.id}
          size="sm"
          class="flex-shrink-0"
        />
        <span class="truncate text-sm text-base-content">
          {@external_user.name || @external_user.email}
        </span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <% external_spaces = @channels ++ @dm_conversations %>
    <nav
      class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2"
      aria-label="Your spaces"
      data-role="external-space-list"
    >
      <%= if external_spaces == [] do %>
        <%!-- Calm zero-allowlist empty state (Saru direction). NEVER the internal
             "browse other channels" new-user hint — that would advertise a
             discovery surface that does not exist for this user. --%>
        <div
          class="flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 text-center"
          data-role="external-empty"
        >
          <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-8 text-base-content/30"></span>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70">Nothing here yet</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50">
            Your conversations will appear here.
          </p>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <.link
          :for={space <- external_spaces}
          patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
          class={[
            "channel-row",
            @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
          ]}
        >
          <span :if={space.kind == "channel"} class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
          <span class="truncate flex-1">
            {if space.kind == "channel",
              do: masked_space_name(assigns, space.name),
              else: sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}
          </span>
          <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
            <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
              {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            </span>
          <% end %>
        </.link>
      <% end %>
    </nav>

    <%!-- External users MAY start DMs to allowlisted humans (the picker is
         filtered to exactly that set in stage 3), so this one affordance stays —
         it is NOT internal-discovery chrome. --%>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click="new_conversation_open"
      aria-label="New conversation"
      data-role="external-new-conversation"
      class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 w-full border-t border-base-300 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors"
      style="padding-bottom: calc(0.5rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));"
    >
      <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
      <span>New conversation</span>
    </button>
  </aside>

  <aside
    :if={!@embedded and !@external?}
    id="chat-sidebar"
    phx-hook="ResizableSidebar"
    class="hidden lg:flex relative flex-shrink-0 flex-col border-r border-base-content/10 bg-base-200"
  >
    <%!-- Sidebar header (chat sidebar Stage 5). Hosts the "Edit layout" /
         "Done" toggle. In edit mode the rail shows per-channel grab handles,
         per-section Hide/Show controls, keyboard move buttons, and a "Reset
         to default layout" action; in normal mode the rail navigates as
         before. Desktop only — the whole aside is `hidden lg:flex`. --%>
    <%!-- Sidebar header. The ~260px rail can't fit two text toggles, so the
         personal "Edit layout" and admin "Edit default" entry points collapse
         into ONE overflow ("More") menu (ui-ux-pro overflow-menu pattern: when
         actions exceed available space, use an overflow menu instead of
         cramming).

         Overflow contract — this row must NEVER push content past the ~260px
         rail in ANY mode. Containment comes from the flex children, NOT from
         clipping the row: the row is `min-w-0`, the text child truncates
         (`flex-1 min-w-0 truncate`), and the action button is pinned
         (`flex-shrink-0`). We deliberately do NOT put `overflow-hidden` on
         this row — the normal-mode "More" popover is anchored inside it and
         opens BELOW it (`top-full`), so an `overflow-hidden` row would clip
         the menu off (it did: the dropdown rendered hidden behind the rail).
           * in EITHER edit mode we do NOT also render the word "CHANNELS" —
             the mode label IS the row's text and takes the remaining space
             (`flex-1 min-w-0 truncate`), with only the "Done" button pinned
             (`flex-shrink-0`). The mode label + accent already say which mode
             is active, so "Done" needs no "(admin)" qualifier;
           * in normal mode the "CHANNELS" label is the flex-1 truncating child
             and the kebab "More" button is pinned (`flex-shrink-0`). --%>
    <div class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 border-b border-base-content/10 min-w-0">
      <%= cond do %>
        <% @sidebar_edit -> %>
          <%!-- In personal-edit mode: a single "Done" exit + a quiet mode
               label that absorbs the row's free space and truncates. No other
               control — and no "CHANNELS" word — occupies the row. --%>
          <span class="channel-edit-mode-label flex-1">Editing my layout</span>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_sidebar_edit"
            class="channel-edit-toggle flex-shrink-0"
            aria-pressed="true"
            aria-label="Done editing layout"
          >
            Done
          </button>
        <% @sidebar_admin_edit -> %>
          <%!-- In admin-edit mode: a single "Done" exit + an admin-accented
               mode label so the admin always knows they are editing what
               everyone sees. The label absorbs free space and truncates; only
               "Done" is pinned. No "CHANNELS" word in the row. --%>
          <span class="channel-edit-mode-label channel-edit-mode-label--admin flex-1">
            Editing company default
          </span>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_sidebar_admin_edit"
            class="channel-admin-edit-toggle flex-shrink-0"
            aria-pressed="true"
            aria-label="Done editing the company default"
          >
            Done
          </button>
        <% true -> %>
          <%!-- Normal mode: the "CHANNELS" label (flex-1, truncates) + ONE
               compact "More" (kebab) button (flex-shrink-0). Clicking the
               button opens an absolutely-positioned popover CONTAINED within
               the aside (the wrapper is position:relative so the menu anchors
               to the header, never floats over the chat pane). The menu closes
               on click-away and Escape; choosing an item enters the mode AND
               closes the menu (handled server-side). --%>
          <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/60">
            Channels
          </p>
          <%!-- Screen-share name masking (task 01a00c66). PERMANENTLY VISIBLE
               in the header row, a sibling of the kebab — never an item inside
               the kebab popover or any other dropdown. Harper's request offered
               "an eye symbol or some other dropdown"; the eye wins because a
               dropdown costs two clicks and a decision at the exact moment
               someone is fumbling with a share dialog.

               Posts the DESIRED next state rather than a flip, so a duplicated
               event from a render race is idempotent (same convention as
               `toggle_section_collapsed`). The icon swap is deliberately NOT
               the feature's signal — see the mode strip below. --%>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_mask_names"
            phx-value-masked={to_string(!@mask_names?)}
            class="channel-mask-toggle flex-shrink-0"
            aria-pressed={to_string(@mask_names?)}
            aria-label="Hide workspace names for sharing"
          >
            <span
              class={[if(@mask_names?, do: "hero-eye-slash", else: "hero-eye"), "size-4"]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
            </span>
          </button>
          <div class="channel-sidebar-menu relative flex-shrink-0">
            <button
              type="button"
              phx-click="toggle_sidebar_menu"
              class="channel-sidebar-menu-button"
              aria-haspopup="menu"
              aria-expanded={to_string(@sidebar_menu_open)}
              aria-label="Sidebar options"
            >
              <span class="hero-ellipsis-vertical size-4"></span>
            </button>
            <div
              :if={@sidebar_menu_open}
              class="channel-sidebar-menu-popover"
              role="menu"
              aria-label="Sidebar options"
              phx-click-away="close_sidebar_menu"
              phx-window-keydown="close_sidebar_menu"
              phx-key="escape"
            >
              <%!-- FIRST, above the layout items: this one acts on the
                    conversations, the other two act on how the rail is
                    arranged. Ordinary menu-row styling on purpose — no
                    warning colour and no confirmation step, because reading
                    a conversation undoes it. --%>
              <button
                type="button"
                role="menuitem"
                phx-click="mark_all_read"
                class="channel-sidebar-menu-item"
              >
                Mark all as read
              </button>
              <button
                type="button"
                role="menuitem"
                phx-click="toggle_sidebar_edit"
                class="channel-sidebar-menu-item"
              >
                Edit my layout
              </button>
              <%!-- Admin-only entry point. Rendered ONLY for Fabrikam admins; the
                   handler re-checks @fabrikam_admin? as the real gate. Admin accent
                   so it reads as a company-wide action, not a personal one. --%>
              <button
                :if={@fabrikam_admin?}
                type="button"
                role="menuitem"
                phx-click="toggle_sidebar_admin_edit"
                class="channel-sidebar-menu-item channel-sidebar-menu-item--admin"
              >
                Edit company default
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%!-- THE MODE STRIP IS THE SIGNAL, NOT THE ICON'S STATE (task 01a00c66).
         An eye and a crossed-out eye differ by a few pixels of stroke, and the
         only moment this feature exists for is a half-second glance under
         social pressure while starting a screen share. Both misreadings cost:
         believing it is on when it is off puts the client list on the call;
         believing it is off when it is on has someone hunting for a client
         that is sitting there as `Workspace C` while people watch. So the
         active mode gets a full-width band, not a glyph state.

         `--color-warning` because this is a deliberate TEMPORARY MODE, which
         is how warning already reads on the notification-state row — not
         `--color-error` (says something is wrong) and not `--color-primary`
         (the action colour; it would read as a button).

         Copy is about PRESENTING, never privacy: nothing here says privacy,
         secure, protected or encrypted, and there is no padlock or shield
         anywhere in this feature — an icon would make the same overclaim the
         forbidden words would. The eye is the only permitted metaphor. --%>
    <div :if={@mask_names?} class="channel-mask-strip">
      <span class="hero-eye-slash size-3.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        {if MapSet.size(@revealed_section_ids) > 0,
          do: "Names hidden · #{MapSet.size(@revealed_section_ids)} showing",
          else: "Names hidden for sharing"}
      </span>
      <button type="button" phx-click="remask_all" class="channel-mask-strip-action">
        Show all
      </button>
    </div>
    <nav
      id="chat-section-list"
      phx-hook="SectionReorder"
      data-sidebar-edit={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
      class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2"
      aria-label="Channel sections"
    >
      <%!-- The Pinned block — ONE list holding pinned channels, pinned DMs
           and pinned task conversations, above every other section in the
           rail.

           It was two adjacent blocks ("Pinned Channels" and "Pinned Tasks")
           until 2026-08-10. Marlowe pinned a task from the Tasks page, went to
           Chat and found its execution log in her rail: pinning a task is the
           same act as pinning a channel, so it is one need and one block. The
           heading is the bare word "Pinned" because the block now holds
           everything that word covers.

           ONE ROW SHAPE, THREE GLYPHS, per Saru's design canvas for task
           019feec6-73d9. Row
           height, name treatment, hover, active state, unread pill and
           truncation are identical across the three kinds; the 20px glyph
           column is the only thing that varies. Deliberately NOT done: kind
           labels, dividers between kinds, per-kind tints, sub-headings. Each
           of those re-states the separation this block exists to remove, and
           in a 260px rail a kind chip is three characters of name.

           Ordering is newest-pinned first, with task rows ABOVE conversation
           rows — see `pinned_rail_entries/2` for why the two halves cannot be
           interleaved and why tasks lead.

           Renders only when non-empty. When empty it renders NOTHING: no
           label, no placeholder. The top of a 260px rail is too expensive to
           spend on instructions for a feature nobody has adopted.

           NO CHROME, per the design canvas: no icon beside the label, no
           surface fill, no border box, no collapse control. Every other
           grouping in the rail earns an affordance; this one earns none,
           and the absence is what makes it read as the user's own rather
           than as another client. A `base-300` rule separates it from what
           follows. NOT hideable, NOT reorderable.

           NO CLIENT COLOUR, and no space held for one. The rail carries
           client colour in section headers only. The row takes exactly the
           left padding of a row in any client section, so the block sits
           flush with the rest of the rail. (Task 019fd810 would have added
           a per-row colour marker and was cancelled; reserved space with
           nothing in it reads as a rendering bug.) --%>
      <%!-- Row-drag scope for the Pinned block (task 019fe987). A SECOND
           mount of the same ChannelMembershipDrag hook, not a second hook:
           the sub-org mount lives further down the rail and an element
           carries one phx-hook, so the block needs its own root. The rows
           below are the only draggables inside it, which is why a drag can
           never move a conversation INTO or OUT OF the block — pinning
           stays a click on the pin control.

           `data-admin-edit` is hard-coded false. There is no org default
           for "what this person pinned", so admin-edit must not turn a
           pinned drag into a global reassignment. --%>
      <% pinned_entries = pinned_rail_entries(@channel_sections.pinned, @pinned_task_spaces) %>
      <%= if pinned_entries != [] do %>
        <div
          id="pinned-row-drag"
          phx-hook="ChannelMembershipDrag"
          data-sidebar-edit={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
          data-admin-edit="false"
        >
          <section
            class="channel-section group border-b border-base-300 pb-2 mb-2"
            data-section-key="pinned"
            data-section-reorderable="false"
            data-row-reorderable="true"
            data-row-scope="pinned"
            aria-label="Pinned"
          >
            <div class="channel-section-header">
              <p class="channel-section-label">Pinned</p>
            </div>
            <%= for %{kind: kind, space: space, move_index: move_index, move_count: move_count} <-
                  pinned_entries do %>
              <%!-- Bound once, used twice: as the row's visible label and as the
                   target inside the row control's accessible name. Resolving a
                   DM's label runs a participants query, so calling the helper
                   at each use would double the block's query count. --%>
              <% row_label = pinned_row_label(kind, space, @user_id) %>
              <%!-- Row wrapper: pairs the navigate-link with the row's own
                   overflow trigger as SIBLINGS, the same shape the sub-org
                   rows use. The wrapper carries the row's margin, rounding and
                   hover/active background (see `.channel-row-wrap` in app.css)
                   so the highlight spans the control too, and the `--active`
                   modifier must ride along or the scoped
                   `.channel-row-wrap > .channel-row--active` rule strips the
                   selected row's tint.

                   `data-role="pinned-task-rail-row-wrap"` survives the merge on
                   task rows only — it is what the task-pin tests address.

                   `data-row-locked` marks a row the drag must route AROUND
                   rather than through: the hook drops locked rows from the
                   order it computes and clamps a drop that lands on one. It is
                   the client half of the rule that `move_index: nil` states on
                   the server. Task rows are the only locked rows today. --%>
              <div
                class={[
                  "channel-row-wrap group/row",
                  @sidebar_edit && "channel-row-wrap--editing",
                  @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row-wrap--active"
                ]}
                data-role={kind == :task && "pinned-task-rail-row-wrap"}
                data-space-id={space.id}
                data-row-locked={kind == :task && "true"}
              >
                <%!-- Grab handle (task 019fe987), borrowed verbatim from the
                     sub-org rows rather than invented here. Rendered ONLY in
                     personal-edit mode, never at rest: the row already carries
                     its overflow trigger on the right edge, and a second
                     permanent control on its left squeezes the name from both
                     sides, which the brand page's truncation rule forbids
                     because the name is the protected fragment.

                     CONVERSATION ROWS ONLY (Marlowe, 2026-08-12: "it's essentially
                     two separate lists so makes me think to not commingle the
                     interactions too much"). A task row is in the block but is
                     not hand-orderable, and the absence of a handle is what says
                     so. `move_index` is nil exactly on those rows.

                     NOT gated on `@sidebar_admin_edit` (unlike the sub-org rows,
                     which drag in either mode). Admin-edit rearranges the org
                     default; a pin list is one person's and has no org default,
                     so there is nothing for an admin to drag here.

                     This span, not the wrapper, carries `draggable` so it is the
                     HTML5 drag SOURCE and the hook's `.channel-row-grab` gate
                     matches. `tabindex` is untouched (a span is not focusable):
                     the keyboard path is the ▲▼ pair below, not this. --%>
                <span
                  :if={@sidebar_edit and move_index != nil}
                  class="channel-row-grab"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  title="Drag to reorder"
                  draggable="true"
                >
                  ⠿
                </span>
                <%!-- The handle's slot, held open on the rows that do not get
                     one, so the names stay in one column when edit mode opens.
                     Same `w-5 ml-1` box `.channel-row-grab` occupies; no new
                     class and no new token for an empty box. --%>
                <span
                  :if={@sidebar_edit and move_index == nil}
                  class="w-5 ml-1 shrink-0"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                </span>
                <.link
                  patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                  data-role={kind == :task && "pinned-task-rail-row"}
                  data-space-id={kind == :task && space.id}
                  class={[
                    "channel-row",
                    @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
                  ]}
                >
                  <%!-- The glyph column: 20px wide, and the ONLY thing that
                       varies between the three kinds.

                       `#` for a channel, an empty slot for a person, and
                       `hero-clipboard-document-list-mini` for a task
                       conversation. All three already existed before the merge;
                       no new marker was designed and none was added.

                       Both glyphs render at `--color-base-content` 60%. The `#`
                       was at 40% and the task glyph at 40% while they lived in
                       separate blocks; side by side in one column, two opacities
                       read as two levels of importance rather than two kinds of
                       thing.

                       The person slot stays EMPTY rather than taking an avatar:
                       `initials/1` takes the first two words of the label, so a
                       group DM named "Rowan Ellis, Alexandra ..." rendered
                       "RM" and was indistinguishable from a private DM with
                       Rowan. It is not the reserved gutter plan v3 rules out —
                       that was space held for a colour marker that is never
                       arriving, whereas a blank beside rows visibly carrying a
                       `#` reads as "no hash here". --%>
                  <%= case kind do %>
                    <% :channel -> %>
                      <span
                        class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center text-base-content/60"
                        data-role="pinned-row-hash"
                      >
                        #
                      </span>
                    <% :dm -> %>
                      <span class="w-5 shrink-0" data-role="pinned-row-indent" aria-hidden="true">
                      </span>
                    <% :task -> %>
                      <%!-- Wrapped in the same `w-5` slot the `#` occupies so
                           the names form one straight column. The glyph itself
                           is 14px like the hash; the box around it is 20px. --%>
                      <span
                        class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center"
                        data-role="pinned-row-task-glyph"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                      >
                        <span class="hero-clipboard-document-list-mini size-3.5 text-base-content/60">
                        </span>
                      </span>
                  <% end %>
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">{row_label}</span>
                  <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                    <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                      {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                    </span>
                  <% end %>
                </.link>
                <%!-- Keyboard and screen-reader reorder path (task 019fe987,
                     WCAG 2.1.1). NOT a touch fallback for the drag above: drag
                     alone is operable by one kind of user with one kind of
                     input, and this rail already carries a logged defect where a
                     hover-gated control was unreachable without a pointer. These
                     ship the same day the drag does.

                     The accessible name carries the VERB AND THE TARGET. A bare
                     "Move up" is meaningless in a list of identical controls, and
                     the block is exactly such a list. No "#" prefix, unlike the
                     sub-org rows: this block holds people too, and a hash on a
                     person names the wrong object type.

                     Boundary buttons are disabled rather than hidden, matching
                     the sub-org rows, so focus order stays stable as a row
                     travels to the top or the bottom. The boundaries are
                     `move_index` against `move_count` — the row's place among
                     the CONVERSATIONS, not among the block's rows. Counting the
                     task rows would leave the ▲ enabled on the top conversation
                     and point it at a destination it is not allowed to have. --%>
                <span :if={@sidebar_edit and move_index != nil} class="channel-row-move-controls">
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-row-move-button"
                    phx-click="move_pinned"
                    phx-value-space_id={space.id}
                    phx-value-direction="up"
                    disabled={move_index == 0}
                    data-role="pinned-move-up"
                    aria-label={"Move #{row_label} up"}
                    title="Move up"
                  >
                    <span class="hero-chevron-up size-3"></span>
                  </button>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-row-move-button"
                    phx-click="move_pinned"
                    phx-value-space_id={space.id}
                    phx-value-direction="down"
                    disabled={move_index == move_count - 1}
                    data-role="pinned-move-down"
                    aria-label={"Move #{row_label} down"}
                    title="Move down"
                  >
                    <span class="hero-chevron-down size-3"></span>
                  </button>
                </span>
                <%!-- ONE trailing control on every row of the block, whatever
                     the row holds. Marlowe, 2026-08-13: "for pinned items, it's a
                     little weird to see an 'x' with 3-dots menu, so we should
                     keep the interaction more consistent and just have a 3-dot
                     menu where one of the actions for a pinned item is to unpin
                     it."

                     This replaces a pair of controls that differed by kind: the
                     conversation rows carried `pin_control/1` wearing an x, and
                     the task rows carried an x of their own, each of them beside
                     the trigger. The two unpins are still different operations
                     in different tables — a conversation unpins through
                     `toggle_pinned` (the user's preferences), a task conversation
                     through `unpin_task_from_chat` (`task_chat_pins`,
                     participant-scoped self-unpin) — and the menu keeps them
                     apart. What is gone is the second control on the row.

                     Marlowe's 2026-08-12 ask for a visible way out of the block is
                     reversed here, by her, with a reason: a row wearing two ways
                     to act on it reads as two different objects. The way out is
                     the menu's first item on every pinned row, task rows
                     included, and it is the only item a task row's menu holds
                     ("task - unpin since it gets pinned from a diff page").

                     A task row's trigger is why `row_actions_dialog/1` resolves
                     its subject through `rail_row_actions_target/6` rather than
                     the sheet's resolver: a task-exec space is in neither
                     `@channels` nor `@dm_conversations`. --%>
                <.row_actions_trigger space_id={space.id} name={row_label} />
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </section>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <%!-- DMs section — always rendered, even when empty (Marlowe: empty
           sections keep their header so the rail's structure is visible).
           Section key: "dms". NOT reorderable (Stage 3) — locked under Pinned. --%>
      <section
        class="channel-section group"
        data-section-key="dms"
        data-section-reorderable="false"
        aria-label="Direct Messages"
      >
        <div class="channel-section-header">
          <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-3.5 text-base-content/60"></span>
          <p class="channel-section-label">Direct Messages</p>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="new_conversation_open"
            class="text-base-content/40 hover:text-primary ml-auto"
            title="New conversation"
          >
            <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <%= if @channel_sections.dms == [] do %>
          <p class="channel-section-empty">
            No conversations yet — direct messages will appear here once you start one.
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <%!-- Row wrapper (stage 3). A DM row was a bare link with a name and
               an unread pill and carried no hover affordance of any kind, so
               the pin control is new here rather than an adjustment. Wrapping
               it moves the row's margin/rounding/hover background onto the
               wrapper (the scoped `.channel-row-wrap > .channel-row` rules)
               and leaves the row's own visible content untouched: still a
               bare display name, no glyph, no avatar. --%>
          <%= for space <- @channel_sections.dms do %>
            <%!-- Bound once (a DM's label costs a participants query) and used
                 as both the visible name and the pin control's target. --%>
            <% row_label = sidebar_row_label(space, @user_id) %>
            <div
              class={[
                "channel-row-wrap",
                @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row-wrap--active"
              ]}
              data-space-id={space.id}
            >
              <.link
                patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                class={[
                  "channel-row",
                  @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
                ]}
              >
                <span class="truncate flex-1">{row_label}</span>
                <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                  <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                    {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                  </span>
                <% end %>
              </.link>
              <%!-- One trigger, no pin (task 019ff8ba stage 1). A DM's menu
                   holds Pin alone: `hide_channel` has no reverse for a DM and
                   a person row has no org filing to move. --%>
              <.row_actions_trigger space_id={space.id} name={row_label} />
            </div>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </section>

      <%!-- Sub-org sections (chat sidebar v3 Stage 4). Rendered from
           `@sidebar_sections` — the org-default sections (one per org,
           `channel_sections` table) merged with the user's personal
           arrangement by `Sidebar.resolve_for_user/2`. Each entry is a
           `%{section, channels}`: `section.name` is the header label,
           `section.color` is the scope token driving the org pill, and
           `channels` are the spaces placed under it by `chat_spaces.org_id`.
           ALWAYS rendered, even when empty — empty sections keep their
           header + an empty-state hint so the rail's structure stays visible.

           Filtered by @scope_filter when set (Stage 4): nil → all sections;
           an atom filter → only the section whose color matches that scope.
           The filter is toggled by clicking the chat-header scope-pill. --%>
      <% visible_sections =
        if is_nil(@scope_filter) do
          @sidebar_sections
        else
          Enum.filter(@sidebar_sections, fn %{section: section} ->
            PlatformWeb.ChatLive.section_scope_atom(section.color) == @scope_filter
          end)
        end %>
      <%!-- Screen-share masking (task 01a00c66). Placeholders are derived from
           the FULL `@sidebar_sections`, not from `visible_sections`, so a scope
           filter narrowing the rail cannot relabel the sections that remain —
           the letter is a fixed position in the rail for the session.

           The display name is merged into each entry ONCE here rather than
           recomputed at each render site, because the name reaches the header
           through several derived strings (`data-section-key`, the section's
           own `aria-label`, the collapse toggle's accessible name, the Hide and
           Reorder labels) and a single missed site leaves the real name in the
           accessibility tree while the visible text reads `Workspace B`. That
           is the failure this feature is most likely to ship with, and it
           passes any test that only inspects rendered text. --%>
      <% mask_ctx =
        Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.context(
          @sidebar_sections,
          @mask_names?,
          @revealed_section_ids
        )

      visible_sections =
        Enum.map(visible_sections, fn %{section: section} = entry ->
          entry
          |> Map.put(:display_name, Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(mask_ctx, section))
          |> Map.put(:revealed?, MapSet.member?(@revealed_section_ids, section.id))
        end) %>
      <%!-- ChannelMembershipDrag wrapper (chat sidebar Stage 5). A SEPARATE
           hook element from the <nav>'s SectionReorder hook: an element can
           only carry one phx-hook, and the two drag behaviors target
           different draggables (channel rows here vs. section headers there).
           Both hooks are bubble-phase listeners; each ignores the other's
           dragstart source, so they coexist on overlapping DOM. The hook is
           inert unless `data-sidebar-edit="true"`, which is the only mode it
           reads now: admin-edit used to hand it a second, cross-org meaning
           via `data-admin-edit`, and that path was retired in favour of the
           explicit "Move to organisation…" action (task 019fd76a). --%>
      <div
        id="channel-membership-drag"
        phx-hook="ChannelMembershipDrag"
        data-sidebar-edit={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
      >
        <%!-- `data-row-reorderable` says rows inside this section may be
             reordered. Separate from `data-section-reorderable`, which answers
             whether the SECTION may be dragged elsewhere and is what the
             SectionReorder hook reads. The Pinned block (task 019fe987)
             reorders its rows while staying locked at the top of the rail, so
             the two answers genuinely differ and one flag cannot carry
             both. --%>
        <%!-- `data-section-slug` follows the LABEL, not the record, while the
             mask is on: the colour token IS the org slug ("wayne-tech"), so an
             unmasked attribute spells the real name in the page source beside a
             header reading `Workspace B` — a leak that any assertion written
             against visible text passes straight over. Nothing reads the
             attribute at runtime (SectionReorder keys off `data-section-id`;
             the dot colour comes from `section_dot_class/1`). --%>
        <section
          :for={
            %{
              section: section,
              channels: section_channels,
              collapsed?: collapsed?,
              display_name: display_name,
              revealed?: revealed?
            } <-
              visible_sections
          }
          id={"section-#{section.id}"}
          class={[
            "channel-section group",
            (@mask_names? and revealed?) && "channel-section--revealed"
          ]}
          data-section-key={display_name}
          data-section-slug={
            if(@mask_names? and not revealed?,
              do: Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.slug(display_name),
              else: section.color
            )
          }
          data-section-id={section.id}
          data-section-reorderable="true"
          data-row-reorderable="true"
          draggable="true"
          aria-label={"#{display_name} channels"}
        >
          <div class="channel-section-header">
            <%!-- Admin-edit (Stage 6): inline rename form per section header.
                 Submitting (Enter / blur via phx-change is intentionally NOT
                 used — we only persist on explicit submit so a mid-typing
                 re-render can't fire a half-typed name). The hidden section_id
                 rides along so the server knows which org-default row to
                 rename. In personal-edit and normal modes the label is static
                 text. --%>
            <%!-- Collapse toggle (019fd80f stage 2). The header is a FLEX ROW
                 whose first child is this button; it is deliberately NOT a
                 wrapper around the whole header, because the header already
                 contains the Hide control and the drag handle and a button
                 inside a button is invalid markup that assistive tech resolves
                 unpredictably. Those two stay siblings of this toggle.

                 Posts the DESIRED next state (`collapsed`) rather than a flip,
                 so a double-fire from a render race is idempotent. The chevron
                 is decorative; the accessible name carries the section so a
                 screen-reader user hearing a list of toggles can tell them
                 apart. In admin-edit the rename input owns the section name, so
                 the toggle carries the chevron alone and the aria-label is the
                 only naming it needs. --%>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-collapse-toggle"
              phx-click="toggle_section_collapsed"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-collapsed={to_string(!collapsed?)}
              aria-expanded={to_string(!collapsed?)}
              aria-label={
                if collapsed?,
                  do: "Expand #{display_name}",
                  else: "Collapse #{display_name}"
              }
            >
              <span
                class={[
                  "channel-section-chevron",
                  if(collapsed?, do: "hero-chevron-right", else: "hero-chevron-down"),
                  "size-3"
                ]}
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
              </span>
              <span
                :if={not @sidebar_admin_edit}
                class="channel-section-label"
              >
                {display_name}
              </span>
            </button>
            <%!-- Admin-edit (Stage 6): inline rename form per section header.
                 Submitting (Enter / blur via phx-change is intentionally NOT
                 used — we only persist on explicit submit so a mid-typing
                 re-render can't fire a half-typed name). The hidden section_id
                 rides along so the server knows which org-default row to
                 rename. In personal-edit and normal modes the label is static
                 text. --%>
            <form
              :if={@sidebar_admin_edit}
              phx-submit="rename_section_default"
              class="channel-section-rename-form"
            >
              <input type="hidden" name="section_id" value={section.id} />
              <input
                type="text"
                name="name"
                value={section.name}
                class="channel-section-rename-input"
                aria-label={"Rename #{section.name} section"}
                maxlength="60"
              />
            </form>
            <%!-- Color-only swatch. The section's IDENTITY text is `section.name`
                 (rendered above / in the rename input); this dot communicates
                 the section's COLOR and nothing else. Previously this slot held
                 a `<.scope_pill>` whose VISIBLE TEXT was derived from the color
                 token via the scope enum, so recoloring a section (e.g. Fabrikam →
                 yellow) silently relabeled the chip to "Paragon". Decoupling:
                 a recolor now changes ONLY this dot, never any name/label. The
                 dot is decorative (aria-hidden) — `section.name` beside it is
                 the text identity. --%>
            <%!-- The span ALWAYS renders (task 01a00910 stage 4). Since buckets
                 derive from the orgs table, a section can carry a colour token
                 the vocabulary has never heard of, and `section_dot_class/1`
                 returns nil for it BY DESIGN — that nil is the signal, not a
                 missing clause, which is why there is no seventh clause over
                 there. Rendering nothing would slide this header's text one
                 dot-width left and ragged-edge the column, making the newest
                 org the one that looks broken; so the slot is reserved and the
                 dot is drawn hollow instead. `aria-hidden` in BOTH branches —
                 the dot is decorative either way, `section.name` is the text
                 identity. --%>
            <span
              class={[
                "channel-section-color-dot",
                PlatformWeb.ChatLive.section_dot_class(section.color) ||
                  "channel-section-color-dot--unassigned"
              ]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
            </span>
            <%!-- Per-item reveal (task 01a00c66). ONE click, no menu: the case
                 this serves is walking one client through their own channel
                 with the rest of the rail still masked. A real focusable
                 button rather than a hover affordance, because
                 `@media (hover: hover)` never matches on a touch device and
                 the control would vanish there entirely. --%>
            <button
              :if={@mask_names? and not revealed?}
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-reveal-button"
              phx-click="reveal_section"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              aria-label="Show this workspace name"
            >
              <span class="hero-eye size-3.5" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
            <%!-- Per-section Hide/Show control (Stage 5, edit mode only).
                 Posts the DESIRED next hidden state so the toggle is
                 idempotent. A hidden section drops out of @sidebar_sections
                 entirely (resolver behavior), so the only way to bring it
                 back is the "Reset to default layout" button below — which
                 is why we never render a Show control inline here. --%>
            <button
              :if={@sidebar_edit}
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-hide-button"
              phx-click="toggle_section_hidden"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-hidden="true"
              aria-label={"Hide #{display_name} section"}
              title="Hide section"
            >
              <span class="hero-eye-slash size-3.5"></span>
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-drag-handle"
              aria-label={"Reorder #{display_name} section"}
              tabindex="-1"
              draggable="true"
            >
              ☰
            </button>
            <%!-- Org archive / schedule-deletion (task 019f4eaa stage 6).
                 Fabrikam-admin only, and only for tenant orgs — the root org's
                 section is never offered (the lifecycle refuses it). --%>
            <.lifecycle_menu
              :if={@fabrikam_admin? and MapSet.member?(@tenant_org_ids, section.org_id)}
              key={"org:#{section.org_id}"}
              open={@lifecycle_menu_key == "org:#{section.org_id}"}
              type="org"
              id={section.org_id}
              name={display_name}
              class="relative ml-auto opacity-0 focus-within:opacity-100 group-hover:opacity-100"
            />
          </div>
          <%!-- Admin-edit (Stage 6): compact recolor palette — the 5 scope
               tokens ARE the palette (no free-form color picker). Each swatch
               posts `recolor_section_default` with the section id + token; the
               active token is marked so the admin sees the current color. The
               server whitelist-validates the token and re-checks fabrikam_admin?
               before writing `channel_sections.color`. --%>
          <div
            :if={@sidebar_admin_edit}
            class="channel-section-palette"
            role="group"
            aria-label={"Set color for #{display_name} section"}
          >
            <button
              :for={token <- ~w(fabrikam soylent wayne-tech sxi paragon cyberdyne)}
              type="button"
              phx-click="recolor_section_default"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-color={token}
              class={[
                "channel-section-swatch",
                "channel-section-swatch--#{token}",
                section.color == token && "channel-section-swatch--active"
              ]}
              aria-pressed={to_string(section.color == token)}
              aria-label={"Color: #{token}"}
              title={token}
            >
            </button>
          </div>
          <%!-- Section body (019fd80f stages 2-3). Collapse is NOT hide — a
               hidden section leaves the rail entirely (the resolver drops it),
               whereas a collapsed one keeps its place, its header and its
               resolved channels. THREE states, not two:

                 * expanded                — every channel row.
                 * collapsed, with activity — header plus only the rows with
                   unread: the "ajar group" below. This is what lets someone
                   keep four clients closed and still see anything that moved.
                 * collapsed, quiet         — header only, an ordinary accordion.

               `section_channel_rows/3` picks the rows and keeps each one's index
               in the FULL channel list, so the keyboard move controls on a
               peeked row still reason about the whole section. --%>
          <% rows = section_channel_rows(section_channels, collapsed?, @unread_counts) %>
          <p :if={not collapsed? and section_channels == []} class="channel-section-empty">
            No channels yet — channels in this org appear here.
          </p>
          <%!-- The ajar group. Peeked rows hang off the collapsed header on a
               2px left rule so they read as one object left ajar rather than as
               loose rows that failed to hide, and the group closes with a quiet
               "Show all (N)" line. Peeked rows are ORDINARY rows — not shrunk,
               dimmed or italicised — because they are the ones a person wants to
               click. There is deliberately no unread rollup on the collapsed
               header: it would restate the pills already visible on the rows
               beneath it. One number, in one place, in the "Show all (N)" line.

               Rendered only when there is something to render: an expanded empty
               section takes the hint above, and a collapsed quiet one takes
               nothing at all. --%>
          <div :if={rows != []} class={collapsed? && "channel-ajar-group"}>
            <div
              :for={{space, idx} <- rows}
              class={[
                "channel-row-wrap",
                (@sidebar_edit || @sidebar_admin_edit) && "channel-row-wrap--editing",
                @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row-wrap--active"
              ]}
              data-channel-id={space.id}
              data-space-id={space.id}
              data-section-id={section.id}
            >
              <%!-- Grab handle — PERSONAL edit only (Stage 5).
                   This span — not the row-wrap — carries draggable so it is the
                   HTML5 drag SOURCE node: dragstart's e.target is then this span,
                   so the ChannelMembershipDrag hook's `.channel-row-grab` gate
                   matches (mirroring SectionReorder, whose handle is the source
                   too). A click on the row link still navigates because the link
                   isn't draggable. tabindex=-1 because the keyboard alternative
                   is the Up/Down buttons.

                   Admin-edit renders NO handle (task 019fd76a stage 2). The
                   gesture used to mean "refile this channel's org for
                   everyone", which is a company-wide act with an invisible
                   consequence — it re-points canvas read access — and it now
                   lives behind the "Move to organisation…" item on the row's
                   overflow menu, with a confirmation dialog. Dragging a row
                   means one thing in one mode: reorder it in my own rail. --%>
              <span
                :if={@sidebar_edit}
                class="channel-row-grab"
                aria-hidden="true"
                title="Drag to move"
                draggable="true"
              >
                ⠿
              </span>
              <.link
                patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                class={[
                  "channel-row",
                  @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
                ]}
              >
                <span class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
                <span class="truncate flex-1">
                  {Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(mask_ctx, section, space.name)}
                </span>
                <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                  <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                    {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                  </span>
                <% end %>
              </.link>
              <%!-- Keyboard move controls (Stage 5, edit mode only — WCAG
                   2.1.1 keyboard alternative to drag). Each posts the same
                   `move_channel` event the keyboard path shares with drag's
                   `channel_moved` persistence. Up is disabled on the first
                   row, Down on the last, so focus can't trigger a no-op
                   that reads as broken. --%>
              <span :if={@sidebar_edit} class="channel-row-move-controls">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-row-move-button"
                  phx-click="move_channel"
                  phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                  phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                  phx-value-direction="up"
                  disabled={idx == 0}
                  aria-label={
                    "Move ##{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(mask_ctx, section, space.name)} up"
                  }
                  title="Move up"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-up size-3"></span>
                </button>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-row-move-button"
                  phx-click="move_channel"
                  phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                  phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                  phx-value-direction="down"
                  disabled={idx == length(section_channels) - 1}
                  aria-label={
                    "Move ##{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(mask_ctx, section, space.name)} down"
                  }
                  title="Move down"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-down size-3"></span>
                </button>
              </span>
              <%!-- The row's only trailing control (task 019ff8ba stage 1,
                   Option C). Pin, "Move to organisation…" and the eye-slash
                   hide button all stood here at rest, on every row of the
                   rail, all the time. Marlowe, 2026-08-13: the pin leaves the
                   row in EVERY mode, not only while arranging.

                   Available in NORMAL mode, for the reason the pin was:
                   pinning is how you use the rail, not an act of rearranging
                   it, and gating it behind "Edit my layout" would put a
                   two-step preamble in front of it.

                   Rows in this section are unpinned by definition — a pinned
                   channel is lifted into the Pinned block above — so the
                   menu's first item is always the Pin direction here. --%>
              <.row_actions_trigger
                space_id={space.id}
                name={Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(mask_ctx, section, space.name)}
              />
            </div>
            <%!-- "Show all (N)": the line that stops a partial list reading as a
                 rendering bug. N is the section's TOTAL channel count, so it
                 answers "where did the rest go" at the moment a person asks it.
                 It is a real focusable control and it doubles as the expand
                 target, posting the same DESIRED-state event as the header
                 toggle. Its accessible name carries the count AND the section
                 because the left rule that groups these rows communicates
                 nothing to a screen reader: without it, someone hearing two
                 channels under a heading has no way to know seven are
                 withheld. --%>
            <button
              :if={collapsed?}
              type="button"
              class="channel-ajar-show-all"
              phx-click="toggle_section_collapsed"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-collapsed="false"
              aria-label={"Show all #{length(section_channels)} channels in #{display_name}"}
            >
              Show all ({length(section_channels)})
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <%!-- Reset to default layout (chat sidebar Stage 5, edit mode only).
           Clears all three per-user override keys (section order, channel
           placement, hidden sections) so the rail returns to the org default
           — the only way to un-hide a section hidden via the per-section
           control above. --%>
      <button
        :if={@sidebar_edit}
        type="button"
        phx-click="reset_sidebar"
        class="channel-reset-layout-button"
        aria-label="Reset to default layout"
      >
        <span class="hero-arrow-path size-4"></span>
        <span>Reset to default layout</span>
      </button>

      <%!-- Brand-new-user empty state — surfaces when the user has no
           channels AND no DMs at all. The sub-org headers above still
           render (with their own empty-state hints), but a separate
           top-level invite chip keeps the "Welcome to Suite" message
           from Stage 1 visible.

           `@archived_channels == []` is part of the test (task 019f4eaa):
           having archived channels is proof you are NOT a brand-new user, so
           "Welcome to Suite. To get started, create a space" is simply wrong
           — it rendered directly above the ARCHIVED section, telling an admin
           who had just archived her orgs that she had never used the product.
           Org-archive made this trivial to hit: it empties every channel in
           an org at once. Hidden channels deliberately do NOT count here —
           `@channels` still carries them (hiding is applied downstream in
           `channel_sections/4`), so hiding everything is not mistaken for
           being new either. --%>
      <.empty_state
        :if={@channels == [] and @dm_conversations == [] and @archived_channels == []}
        variant={:conversational}
      >
        <:system_message>— no spaces yet —</:system_message>
        <:body>Welcome to Suite. To get started, create a space or connect your agent.</:body>
        <:chips label="+ Create a space" event="new_channel_open" />
        <:chips label="+ Connect an agent" event={JS.navigate(~p"/control")} />
      </.empty_state>

      <%!-- Archived channels (task 019e95ea stage 2). Renders only when at
           least one archived channel exists; collapsed by default with a
           phx-click toggle (same idea as the hidden-channels drawer below —
           quiet until asked for). Rows stay OUT of @channel_sections /
           @sidebar_sections: archived channels never mix into the active
           buckets, they only live here. Muted treatment mirrors the
           hidden-channels rows; the row still navigates so the read-only
           snapshot stays reachable. --%>
      <section
        :if={@archived_channels != []}
        class="channel-section"
        data-section-key="archived"
        data-section-reorderable="false"
        aria-label="Archived channels"
      >
        <button
          type="button"
          class="channel-section-header w-full text-left"
          phx-click="toggle_archived_section"
          aria-expanded={if @archived_open, do: "true", else: "false"}
          aria-controls="archived-channel-list"
        >
          <span class="hero-archive-box size-3.5 text-base-content/40"></span>
          <p class="channel-section-label">Archived</p>
          <span class="ml-auto text-base-content/40 text-xs">
            {if @archived_open, do: "▾", else: "▸"}
          </span>
        </button>
        <div :if={@archived_open} id="archived-channel-list">
          <.link
            :for={space <- @archived_channels}
            patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
            class={[
              "channel-row text-base-content/50",
              @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="hero-archive-box size-3.5 text-base-content/30"></span>
            <span class="truncate flex-1">{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}</span>
          </.link>
        </div>
      </section>
    </nav>

    <%!-- Undo toast — ephemeral 4-second affordance shown after a hide
         (Stage 3 v3 follow-up per Marlowe's 2026-05-29 review). Lives as
         an IN-FLOW `flex-shrink-0` sibling between the scrolling `<nav>`
         (`flex-1`) above and the pinned "+ New channel" button below.
         When the toast appears, the `flex-1` scroll nav absorbs its
         height by shrinking — so "+ New channel" stays exactly where it
         is, the drawer stays exactly where it is, and the toast doesn't
         overlap any content. Trades a soft scroll-area compression for
         stable pinned chrome (the right exchange — overlap with content
         is the actual user complaint; transient scroll compression is
         the standard chat-rail behavior, same way Slack/Discord handle
         compose-area system notes).

         role=status + aria-live=polite (NOT assertive) — hiding a
         channel is non-destructive (nothing deleted, only user-filtered)
         so a polite announcement is the right WCAG choice. The Undo
         button shares its handler with the drawer's Show buttons via
         do_unhide/2 in the LiveView, so the round-trip is identical
         regardless of which way the user reverses the hide. Auto-clears
         via a Process.send_after → handle_info({:clear_undo_toast,
         space_id}) pair scheduled by the hide_channel handler.

         HIDE ONLY. Task 019ffc5f stage 2 gave this toast a second variant
         for the DM Close action, and stage 3 gave that variant a second
         line teaching the rule that brings the row back. Marlowe rejected it
         at the stage-3 gate: "We don't need a acknowledgement / affirmation
         for a close action on a DM. A User can simply search for a person
         or agent to DM again if they want to bring back the window." So a
         close now passes silently and this element is back to the single
         verb it shipped with. Hide keeps it because Hide's reverse is a
         drawer, and the toast is the only thing that says the drawer now
         has something in it. --%>
    <div
      :if={@undo_toast}
      role="status"
      aria-live="polite"
      class="channel-undo-toast"
    >
      <span class="channel-undo-toast-message">
        Hidden <span class="font-medium">#{@undo_toast.name}</span>
      </span>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="channel-undo-toast-button"
        phx-click="undo_hide"
        phx-value-id={@undo_toast.space_id}
      >
        Undo
      </button>
    </div>

    <%!-- Move confirmation (task 019ffcad stage 4, from the design canvas).
         Says what just happened after a Fabrikam admin files a channel into
         another organisation. Stages 1 to 3 put the row in its new section
         and make it visible there; the admin is looking at the section it
         LEFT, where the only observable event is a row disappearing.

         The hide toast's component, its position, and its 4s dismissal, with
         the copy and the handler changed and no action button. Undo is out of
         scope for this stage: the move already carries a two-step confirmation
         and the row's own menu moves the channel back in one click. Marlowe's
         separate decision to offer an Undo here is task
         01a01052-3155-7c15-8c48-9ff8955b9b70.

         A SEPARATE assign from `@undo_toast`. Hide and Move are two verbs a
         person can perform seconds apart, and sharing one assign would have
         whichever came second silently blank the first, which is invisible to
         any test that fires only one of them.

         Both names in one sentence. "Moved #gen-migration." leaves the reader
         checking where it went, which is the work this line exists to save.
         The destination is the SECTION's name, so the sentence echoes the word
         the admin just clicked in the chooser (an admin can rename a section
         away from its org's name).

         `channel-move-toast-message` instead of `channel-undo-toast-message`:
         the same flex slot WITHOUT `truncate`. The rail is ~224px wide, and a
         two-name sentence under `truncate` ellipsises from the right, which
         eats the destination: the exact half the copy rule exists to keep. It
         wraps to two lines instead, as the canvas wireframe draws it. The
         toast SURFACE is untouched, so Hide's toast is unchanged.

         Desktop only, like the hide toast: there is no mobile-drawer copy of
         either. --%>
    <div
      :if={@move_toast}
      data-role="channel-move-toast"
      role="status"
      aria-live="polite"
      class="channel-undo-toast"
    >
      <span class="channel-move-toast-message">
        Moved #{@move_toast.channel_name} to {@move_toast.section_name}.
      </span>
    </div>

    <%!-- "+ New channel" — pinned rail chrome (Stage 3 v3 follow-up per
         Marlowe's review). Lives as an UNCONDITIONAL `flex-shrink-0` sibling
         of `<nav>` and the conditional bottom-region wrapper, so its
         visual position never drifts based on channel count OR on whether
         the undo toast / hidden drawer happens to be showing. The wrapper
         was deliberately NOT merged into the bottom-region's `:if` block —
         doing so would yank the button out of view whenever both toast
         and drawer are absent, reintroducing the "position depends on
         state" bug. Visual divider above is a top border using the same
         `border-base-content/10` token the aside itself uses, so the
         rail's separator language stays consistent. Reuses the
         channel-row hover/text vocabulary so the button rhymes visually
         with the section rows above. --%>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click="new_channel_open"
      aria-label="New channel"
      class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 w-full border-t border-base-content/10 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors"
    >
      <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
      <span>New channel</span>
    </button>

    <%!-- Bottom region (Stage 3 v3): hosts the global "N hidden channels"
         drawer ONLY. Silent at N=0 — the wrapper is :if-gated to
         `hidden_count > 0` so it disappears entirely when the user has
         no hidden channels, keeping the sidebar foot empty in the clean
         state. The undo toast used to live here too but moved up to its
         own in-flow position above "+ New channel" — keeps pinned chrome
         (+ New channel, drawer trigger) stable when a hide fires, since
         the scroll-nav (flex-1) absorbs the toast's height instead. --%>
    <% hidden_count =
      @channel_sections.hidden_sub_orgs
      |> Map.values()
      |> Enum.map(&length/1)
      |> Enum.sum() %>
    <div
      :if={hidden_count > 0}
      class="flex-shrink-0 border-t border-base-content/10 px-2 py-2"
    >
      <%!-- Global "N hidden channels" drawer (Option B per Marlowe's v3
           review). One quiet row at the rail's foot — silent at N=0 —
           expanding upward into a scrollable grouped list. The panel
           ALWAYS renders so the max-height CSS transition animates in
           and out smoothly; the `--open` modifier on the wrapper drives
           the transition. Internal scroll caps the panel at min(50vh,
           360px) so it can't claim more than half the sidebar at very
           high hidden counts. Each Show button shares the unhide_channel
           handler with the (now-removed) v2 inline list, so behavior is
           identical to v2 — only the trigger surface changed. --%>
      <div
        :if={hidden_count > 0}
        class={[
          "channel-hidden-drawer",
          @hidden_drawer_open && "channel-hidden-drawer--open"
        ]}
      >
        <div
          id="hidden-drawer-panel"
          class="channel-hidden-drawer-panel"
          aria-hidden={if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "false", else: "true"}
        >
          <%= for {bucket, hidden_channels} <- @channel_sections.hidden_sub_orgs,
                  hidden_channels != [] do %>
            <div class="channel-hidden-drawer-group">
              <div class="channel-hidden-drawer-group-label">
                <%!-- Buckets derive from the orgs table (task 01a00910 stage
                     3), so a bucket can name an org that has no scope colour
                     token. `sub_org_scope_atom/1` returns nil for those and
                     we label the group with its plain name — `scope_pill`'s
                     colour/label clauses are a closed enum and would crash on
                     an unknown scope. --%>
                <% scope = sub_org_scope_atom(bucket)

                hidden_mask_ctx =
                  Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.context(
                    @sidebar_sections,
                    @mask_names?,
                    @revealed_section_ids
                  )

                bucket_label =
                  Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label_for_bucket(
                    hidden_mask_ctx,
                    @sidebar_sections,
                    bucket
                  ) %>
                <%!-- Screen-share masking (task 01a00c66 stage 3). This heading
                     is an ORG NAME, so it masks like every other one — a rail
                     reading `Workspace B` above a hidden-channels group reading
                     the real name has leaked exactly what the mode hides. The
                     placeholder is passed IN; `scope_pill` holds no mask table
                     of its own, because a second copy drifts and the copy that
                     drifts is the one nobody is looking at. --%>
                <.scope_pill
                  :if={scope}
                  scope={scope}
                  clickable={false}
                  label={@mask_names? && bucket_label}
                />
                <span
                  :if={is_nil(scope)}
                  class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/50"
                >
                  {bucket_label}
                </span>
              </div>
              <ul class="channel-hidden-drawer-group-list">
                <li
                  :for={space <- hidden_channels}
                  class="channel-hidden-drawer-item"
                >
                  <span class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}</span>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-hidden-drawer-show"
                    phx-click="unhide_channel"
                    phx-value-id={space.id}
                    aria-label={"Show ##{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}"}
                  >
                    Show
                  </button>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="channel-hidden-drawer-trigger"
          phx-click="toggle_hidden_drawer"
          aria-expanded={if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "true", else: "false"}
          aria-controls="hidden-drawer-panel"
          aria-label={
            if @hidden_drawer_open,
              do: "Collapse hidden channels",
              else: "Show #{hidden_count} hidden channels"
          }
        >
          <span class="flex-1 text-left">
            {hidden_count} hidden {if hidden_count == 1, do: "channel", else: "channels"}
          </span>
          <span class="channel-hidden-drawer-caret">
            {if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "▾", else: "▴"}
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%!-- Drag handle for sidebar resize --%>
    <div
      class="absolute right-0 inset-y-0 w-1 cursor-col-resize hover:bg-primary/40 active:bg-primary/60 transition-colors z-10"
      aria-hidden="true"
    />
  </aside>

  <%!-- Mobile channel browser overlay — suppressed when embedded, and for
       external users (rbac-external-users M5): its sectioned org-tree browser,
       new-channel affordance, and scope-pills are all internal-discovery chrome.
       The external rail above is the single flat surface for those users. --%>
  <%= if @mobile_browser_open and !@embedded and !@external? do %>
    <div
      id="mobile-channel-browser"
      class="fixed inset-0 z-40 flex flex-col bg-base-100 lg:hidden safe-area-x"
    >
      <%!-- Masking context for the drawer (task 01a00c66 stage 3). Derived
           from the FULL `@sidebar_sections` exactly as the rail's is, so a
           section carries the SAME letter on both breakpoints and an active
           search cannot relabel what remains. Built once and threaded to
           every derived string below — the header text, the section's own
           aria-label, both move buttons, the touch drag handle and the
           channel rows — because the way this ships broken is one missed
           site leaving the real name in the accessibility tree under a
           heading that reads `Workspace B`. --%>
      <% drawer_mask_ctx =
        Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.context(
          @sidebar_sections,
          @mask_names?,
          @revealed_section_ids
        ) %>
      <header class="flex h-12 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b border-base-300 px-4 safe-area-top">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Conversations</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
          <%!-- Screen-share name masking on the DRAWER (task 01a00c66 stage 3).
               The SAME control and the SAME event as the desktop rail, not a
               reduced variant: the rail renders at two breakpoints and they
               have diverged before, and a phone that can only reveal — or only
               mask — is the failure this stage exists to prevent. Sized to the
               drawer's 44px touch floor rather than the rail's 16px glyph. --%>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_mask_names"
            phx-value-masked={to_string(!@mask_names?)}
            class="channel-mask-toggle flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 min-w-11 rounded-lg text-base-content/70 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content"
            aria-pressed={to_string(@mask_names?)}
            aria-label="Hide workspace names for sharing"
          >
            <span
              class={[if(@mask_names?, do: "hero-eye-slash", else: "hero-eye"), "size-5"]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
            </span>
          </button>
          <%!-- Mobile entry into personal-edit mode (chat sidebar mobile
               Stage 3). Stage 2's report flagged that `@sidebar_edit` — which
               gates the lock affordances AND this stage's drag handles — was
               only reachable via the desktop rail's kebab menu, hidden on
               phones. This button closes that gap using the SAME
               `toggle_sidebar_edit` event (one edit mode, two entry points).
               Admin-edit stays desktop-only chrome. --%>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_sidebar_edit"
            class="flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 min-w-11 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content"
            aria-pressed={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
            aria-label={if @sidebar_edit, do: "Done editing layout", else: "Edit layout"}
          >
            {if @sidebar_edit, do: "Done", else: "Edit"}
          </button>
          <button
            phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
            class="flex items-center justify-center size-10 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content"
            aria-label="Close"
          >
            <span class="hero-x-mark size-5"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </header>

      <%!-- Drawer search (mobile channel search Stage 1). Pinned row BETWEEN
           the header and the scrolling list — the h-12 header is already full
           (title + Edit/Done + X) and touch targets need breathing room.
           Filters the rendered list as you type via the drawer_filter_*
           helpers; find-verbs ("Find a channel or DM") to stay verbally
           distinct from the DM "+" people-picker, which STARTS conversations.
           text-base is load-bearing: anything under 16px makes iOS auto-zoom
           the viewport on focus. Stable id so LiveView patches preserve
           focus/cursor while the list under it re-renders. --%>
      <div class="flex-shrink-0 px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-300" role="search">
        <%!-- phx-change (NOT phx-keyup): change fires for every way text can
             enter the field — typing, paste, iOS dictation, the native
             type=search clear — where keyup only sees physical keys.
             phx-submit reuses the same handler so the iOS "go" key doesn't
             fall through to a full-page form POST. --%>
        <form class="relative" phx-change="drawer_search" phx-submit="drawer_search">
          <span
            class="hero-magnifying-glass absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 size-4 text-base-content/40"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
          </span>
          <%!-- DrawerSearchFocus (Stage 2): focuses this field on mount when
               the open carried search intent (data attr below), and blurs it
               when the user starts scrolling the list so one swipe drops the
               keyboard. Focus is hook-driven, NOT the HTML autofocus attr —
               autofocus no-ops on iOS when the render lands after a LiveView
               round-trip, outside the tap's gesture chain. --%>
          <input
            id="drawer-search-input"
            type="search"
            name="value"
            value={@drawer_query}
            phx-hook="DrawerSearchFocus"
            data-search-intent={to_string(@drawer_search_intent)}
            phx-debounce="150"
            placeholder="Find a channel or DM"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocorrect="off"
            autocapitalize="none"
            spellcheck="false"
            enterkeyhint="go"
            aria-label="Find a channel or direct message"
            class="w-full h-11 rounded-lg bg-base-200 border border-base-content/10 pl-9 pr-11 text-base placeholder:text-base-content/40 focus:border-primary focus:outline-none"
          />
          <button
            :if={@drawer_query != ""}
            type="button"
            phx-click="drawer_search_clear"
            class="absolute right-0 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 min-w-11 text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content"
            aria-label="Clear search"
          >
            <span class="hero-x-mark size-4"></span>
          </button>
        </form>
      </div>

      <%!-- The mode strip, identical in copy and colour to the rail's (task
           01a00c66 stage 3). It is the signal on this breakpoint too: the icon
           swap is a few pixels of stroke either way, and the phone is the
           likelier device to be mirrored into a call. --%>
      <div :if={@mask_names?} class="channel-mask-strip">
        <span class="hero-eye-slash size-3.5 flex-shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
          {if MapSet.size(@revealed_section_ids) > 0,
            do: "Names hidden · #{MapSet.size(@revealed_section_ids)} showing",
            else: "Names hidden for sharing"}
        </span>
        <button type="button" phx-click="remask_all" class="channel-mask-strip-action">
          Show all
        </button>
      </div>

      <%!-- Sectioned mobile channel browser — parity with the desktop rail
           (chat sidebar mobile Stage 1). Renders the SAME already-computed
           data desktop consumes — `@channel_sections.pinned` / `.dms` and the
           resolver-driven `@sidebar_sections` sub-org list — in the same
           top-to-bottom order: Pinned (locked at top, only when non-empty),
           Direct Messages (locked directly under Pinned), then the sub-org
           sections alphabetically. No new server assign or query — the overlay
           just re-renders the existing assigns with the overlay's touch-sized
           rows. Sub-org sections carry `data-section-id` + reorderable markers
           for the later touch-reorder stage; Pinned + DMs are locked
           (`data-section-reorderable="false"`). We deliberately DON'T set an
           HTML `id` on the sub-org sections: the desktop rail (present in the
           same DOM, hidden via `lg:flex`) already owns `id="section-#{id}"`, so
           a duplicate id here would break LiveView DOM patching. The drawer
           still closes only via the explicit close control + backdrop tap —
           no swipe-to-dismiss.

           SectionReorderTouch (Stage 3) owns long-press + drag reorder for
           the sub-org sections via Pointer Events — the desktop
           SectionReorder hook is HTML5 DnD and never fires on touch. The id
           is required for the hook and must differ from the desktop nav's
           `chat-section-list` (both are in the DOM at once). --%>
      <nav
        id="mobile-section-list"
        phx-hook="SectionReorderTouch"
        data-search-active={to_string(@drawer_query != "")}
        class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2"
        aria-label="Channel sections"
      >
        <%!-- RowReorderTouch (channel-row reorder Stage 2) needs its own
             hook element — one element = one phx-hook, and the nav above is
             owned by SectionReorderTouch. This wrapper is that element; it
             deliberately spans the same subtree so both hooks see every
             pointerdown, each arming only on its own handle class
             (.channel-section-drag-handle vs .channel-row-drag-handle).
             data-search-active mirrors the nav's — same guard rail, read by
             the shared engine on its own root. --%>
        <div
          id="mobile-row-reorder-scope"
          phx-hook="RowReorderTouch"
          data-search-active={to_string(@drawer_query != "")}
        >
          <%!-- Edit-mode explainer (2026-07-09): the ▲▼ buttons are visible
             and self-explanatory, but the hold-to-drag gesture has no visual
             affordance beyond the ☰ glyph — one muted line teaches it. --%>
          <p
            :if={@sidebar_edit && @drawer_query == ""}
            class="px-4 pb-2 text-xs text-base-content/40"
          >
            Reorder with the arrows, or press and hold ☰ to drag.
          </p>
          <%!-- Reorder announcements for screen readers (Stage 3). The
             region renders (empty) as soon as edit mode opens — aria-live
             only announces CHANGES to an existing region, so it must be in
             the DOM before the first move updates it. --%>
          <div :if={@sidebar_edit} class="sr-only" aria-live="polite">
            {@drawer_reorder_announcement}
          </div>
          <%!-- Pinned — locked at the top, rendered only when non-empty
             (and, while searching, only when it has a match).

             ONE section, matching the desktop rail: pinned channels, pinned
             DMs and pinned task conversations in one list with one heading.
             It was two adjacent sections until 2026-08-10. A rename or a
             merge on one surface only is a change a phone user never sees. --%>
          <% drawer_pinned =
            drawer_filter_pinned(
              pinned_rail_entries(@channel_sections.pinned, @pinned_task_spaces),
              @drawer_query,
              @user_id
            ) %>
          <section :if={drawer_pinned != []} data-section-reorderable="false" aria-label="Pinned">
            <div class="flex items-center px-4 py-1">
              <%!-- Same label as the desktop block. Holds all three kinds. --%>
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                Pinned
              </p>
              <%!-- Lock affordance (chat sidebar mobile Stage 2, Decision #5).
                 Touch has no hover state to reveal that Pinned is locked to the
                 top, so we surface an explicit hero-lock-closed icon in edit
                 mode (`@sidebar_edit`, the same personal-edit mode that gates
                 desktop section reorder). The SECTION drag handle stays omitted
                 — mirroring desktop's data-section-reorderable="false" branch,
                 which renders no .channel-section-drag-handle on locked
                 sections.

                 Copy revised (task 019fe987): this used to read "and can't be
                 reordered", which is now false at row level. The block stays
                 pinned to the top of the drawer; the rows inside it reorder. --%>
              <span
                :if={@sidebar_edit}
                class="channel-section-lock hero-lock-closed ml-auto size-3.5 text-base-content/40"
                aria-hidden="true"
                title="Pinned stays at the top of the list"
              >
              </span>
            </div>
            <%!-- EDIT-MODE pinned rows (task 019fe987). Both surfaces or
                 neither: the parent task shipped a stage that wired the desktop
                 rail and left the drawer rendering rows that could not do the
                 thing, and it reached a human approval gate before anyone
                 noticed.

                 Shape copied from the sub-org edit rows directly below, so the
                 drawer teaches ONE arranging convention. That means: the row
                 stops being a link (a mis-tap would navigate and close the
                 drawer, ejecting the user from the mode), the ▲▼ pair is
                 persistent rather than revealed, boundary buttons are disabled
                 rather than hidden, and the unread badge yields its right-edge
                 slot to the reorder chrome because edit mode is a mode and
                 counts are browse chrome.

                 TASK ROWS STAY, and stay unarranged (Marlowe, 2026-08-12: "it's
                 essentially two separate lists so makes me think to not
                 commingle the interactions too much"). They render in the same
                 list with the same glyph column and NO ▲▼ pair, so edit mode
                 shows the block a phone user actually has rather than a
                 filtered version of it. `move_index` is nil on exactly those
                 rows.

                 No ☰ drag handle here, unlike the sub-org rows. Touch drag is
                 the desktop drag's twin and the arrows are the accessible path;
                 the block is three to eight rows, where two taps does the job.
                 If phone users reach for the gesture, adding it is a second
                 mount of RowReorderTouch, not a new pattern.

                 Search suppresses the mode: reordering a filtered view writes
                 an order the user cannot see. Same guard the sub-org rows and
                 the section handles use, and it is what keeps `move_index`
                 contiguous — the indices describe the unfiltered block. --%>
            <%= if @sidebar_edit && @drawer_query == "" do %>
              <div
                :for={
                  %{kind: kind, space: space, move_index: move_index, move_count: move_count} <-
                    drawer_pinned
                }
                class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm"
                data-role={
                  if kind == :task,
                    do: "drawer-pinned-task-edit-row",
                    else: "drawer-pinned-edit-row"
                }
                data-space-id={space.id}
              >
                <% row_label = pinned_row_label(kind, space, @user_id) %>
                <%!-- Same three-glyph column as the browse rows below and as the
                     desktop rail, so a row does not change kind when the mode
                     changes. --%>
                <%= case kind do %>
                  <% :channel -> %>
                    <span
                      class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center text-base-content/60 text-lg"
                      data-role="pinned-row-hash"
                    >
                      #
                    </span>
                  <% :dm -> %>
                    <span class="w-5 shrink-0" data-role="pinned-row-indent" aria-hidden="true">
                    </span>
                  <% :task -> %>
                    <span
                      class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center"
                      data-role="pinned-row-task-glyph"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                    >
                      <span class="hero-clipboard-document-list-mini size-4 text-base-content/60">
                      </span>
                    </span>
                <% end %>
                <span class="truncate flex-1">{row_label}</span>
                <%!-- Boundaries are the row's place among the CONVERSATIONS
                     (`move_index` against `move_count`), not among the block's
                     rows. Counting the task rows above would leave the ▲
                     enabled on the top conversation and point it at a
                     destination it is not allowed to have. --%>
                <span :if={move_index != nil} class="channel-row-move-controls--touch">
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-row-move-button--touch"
                    phx-click="move_pinned"
                    phx-value-space_id={space.id}
                    phx-value-direction="up"
                    disabled={move_index == 0}
                    data-role="pinned-move-up"
                    aria-label={"Move #{row_label} up"}
                    title="Move up"
                  >
                    <span class="hero-chevron-up size-4"></span>
                  </button>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-row-move-button--touch"
                    phx-click="move_pinned"
                    phx-value-space_id={space.id}
                    phx-value-direction="down"
                    disabled={move_index == move_count - 1}
                    data-role="pinned-move-down"
                    aria-label={"Move #{row_label} down"}
                    title="Move down"
                  >
                    <span class="hero-chevron-down size-4"></span>
                  </button>
                </span>
              </div>
            <% else %>
              <%!-- Row wrapper: SIBLING link + trailing control, so a tap on
                 the control never bubbles into the anchor's navigation. A
                 `<button>` nested in an `<a>` is invalid HTML, and LiveView
                 binds click on `window` in the bubble phase, so a nested
                 control would need a `stopPropagation` guard that swallows
                 the navigation too.

                 WHICH control depends on the kind, and this is where the two
                 pin models met. A conversation row carries the overflow
                 control from task 019fe998, which opens the pin/unpin/hide
                 sheet. That control is the only touch path to any of those
                 three: all of them are `group-hover/row:` gated on desktop,
                 and Tailwind compiles `hover:` inside `@media (hover: hover)`,
                 so none of them match on a touch device.

                 A task row keeps its own unpin button instead.
                 `row_actions_target/5` resolves the sheet's subject against
                 `@channels ++ @dm_conversations`, and a task-exec space is in
                 neither list, so the sheet would open on a nil target: empty
                 header, dead actions. The verbs are wrong for it besides. A
                 task pin lives in `task_chat_pins` and comes off through
                 `unpin_task_from_chat`, not through the user's
                 `toggle_pinned` preferences.

                 Neither control carries `phx-click="close_mobile_browser"`,
                 on purpose: opening the sheet must not collapse the drawer
                 out from under it, and unpinning must not collapse it
                 mid-tap. --%>
              <div
                :for={%{kind: kind, space: space} <- drawer_pinned}
                class="flex items-center"
                data-role={
                  if kind == :task, do: "pinned-task-drawer-row-wrap", else: "drawer-row-wrap"
                }
                data-space-id={space.id}
              >
                <% row_label = pinned_row_label(kind, space, @user_id) %>
                <.link
                  patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                  phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
                  data-role={kind == :task && "pinned-task-drawer-row"}
                  data-space-id={kind == :task && space.id}
                  class={[
                    "flex items-center gap-3 flex-1 min-w-0 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
                    "hover:bg-base-200",
                    @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
                      "bg-base-200 text-primary font-semibold"
                  ]}
                >
                  <%!-- The glyph column, same three glyphs as the desktop rail
                     and the only thing that varies between the kinds. Before
                     the kind branch existed the row rendered `{space.name}`
                     for everything, and a DM has no `name`, so a pinned person
                     appeared as a `#` with no label: an unnamed CHANNEL, the
                     wrong object type rather than a missing string. --%>
                  <%= case kind do %>
                    <% :channel -> %>
                      <span
                        class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center text-base-content/60 text-lg"
                        data-role="pinned-row-hash"
                      >
                        #
                      </span>
                    <% :dm -> %>
                      <span class="w-5 shrink-0" data-role="pinned-row-indent" aria-hidden="true">
                      </span>
                    <% :task -> %>
                      <span
                        class="w-5 shrink-0 text-center"
                        data-role="pinned-row-task-glyph"
                        aria-hidden="true"
                      >
                        <span class="hero-clipboard-document-list-mini size-4 text-base-content/60">
                        </span>
                      </span>
                  <% end %>
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">{row_label}</span>
                  <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                    <span class="ml-1 flex-shrink-0 min-w-[1.125rem] h-[1.125rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.6rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center px-1 leading-none">
                      {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                    </span>
                  <% end %>
                </.link>
                <%= if kind == :task do %>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="flex-shrink-0 inline-flex items-center justify-center w-10 h-10 mr-2 rounded text-base-content/40 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors"
                    phx-click="unpin_task_from_chat"
                    phx-value-task-id={space.metadata["task_id"]}
                    data-role="pinned-task-drawer-unpin"
                    data-space-id={space.id}
                    aria-label={"Unpin #{row_label} from Chat"}
                    title="Unpin from Chat"
                  >
                    <span class="hero-x-mark size-4"></span>
                  </button>
                <% else %>
                  <.row_actions_control space_id={space.id} name={row_label} />
                <% end %>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </section>

          <%!-- Direct Messages — locked directly under Pinned. While a search
             is active the whole section hides when no DM display-name
             matches; the "No conversations yet" copy below is ONLY for a
             genuinely DM-less account, never for a no-match search. --%>
          <section
            :if={
              @drawer_query == "" or
                drawer_filter_dms(@channel_sections.dms, @drawer_query, @user_id) != []
            }
            data-section-reorderable="false"
            aria-label="Direct Messages"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-1 mt-2">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                  Direct Messages
                </p>
                <%!-- Lock affordance (chat sidebar mobile Stage 2, Decision #5) —
                   Direct Messages is locked directly under Pinned and can't be
                   reordered; surfaced explicitly for touch (no hover) in edit
                   mode. Drag handle stays omitted, mirroring desktop's
                   data-section-reorderable="false" branch. --%>
                <span
                  :if={@sidebar_edit}
                  class="channel-section-lock hero-lock-closed size-3.5 text-base-content/40"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  title="Direct Messages is locked and can't be reordered"
                >
                </span>
              </div>
              <button
                phx-click={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
                class="flex items-center justify-center size-11 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-primary"
                aria-label="New conversation"
                title="New conversation"
              >
                <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
              </button>
            </div>
            <%!-- Edit-mode caption (channel-row reorder Stage 1): DM rows are
               deliberately NOT reorderable — recency ordering is automatic
               and self-healing, and a manual order would be silently wiped
               by the next incoming message. One line of copy explains the
               absent affordance instead of per-row lock icons. --%>
            <p :if={@sidebar_edit} class="px-4 pb-1 text-xs text-base-content/40">
              Sorted by recent activity
            </p>
            <%= if @channel_sections.dms == [] do %>
              <p class="px-4 py-2 text-sm text-base-content/50">
                No conversations yet — direct messages will appear here once you start one.
              </p>
            <% else %>
              <%!-- Row wrapper (task 019fe998) — see the Pinned block above for
                   why the control is a sibling of the link, never a child. --%>
              <div
                :for={space <- drawer_filter_dms(@channel_sections.dms, @drawer_query, @user_id)}
                class="flex items-center"
                data-role="drawer-row-wrap"
                data-space-id={space.id}
              >
                <% row_label = sidebar_row_label(space, @user_id) %>
                <.link
                  patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                  phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
                  class={[
                    "flex flex-1 min-w-0 items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
                    "hover:bg-base-200",
                    @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
                      "bg-base-200 text-primary font-semibold"
                  ]}
                >
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">{row_label}</span>
                  <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                    <span class="ml-1 flex-shrink-0 min-w-[1.125rem] h-[1.125rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.6rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center px-1 leading-none">
                      {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                    </span>
                  <% end %>
                </.link>
                <.row_actions_control space_id={space.id} name={row_label} />
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </section>

          <%!-- Sub-org sections — the resolver output (`@sidebar_sections`, the
             same list desktop iterates), rendered in the SAME resolver order as
             desktop (the user's saved drag-order via chat_section_order, then
             admin default). Deliberately NOT re-sorted alphabetically: a hard
             alphabetical sort would override the per-user order that Stage 3's
             touch drag-reorder persists, making that reorder look broken on
             mobile. Keyed by `data-section-id` for the later touch-reorder stage. --%>
          <%!-- While searching, sections render their MATCHING channels only and
             zero-match sections drop out entirely (drawer_filter_sections).
             The neighbor-index math for the move buttons stays valid because
             the edit controls are hidden whenever a search is active — the
             filtered list and @sidebar_sections are identical when the
             controls can actually render. --%>
          <section
            :for={
              {%{section: section, channels: section_channels}, section_index} <-
                Enum.with_index(
                  drawer_filter_sections(@sidebar_sections, @drawer_query, drawer_mask_ctx)
                )
            }
            data-section-id={section.id}
            data-section-reorderable="true"
            aria-label={"#{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(drawer_mask_ctx, section)} channels"}
          >
            <div class="flex items-center px-4 py-1 mt-2">
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                {Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(drawer_mask_ctx, section)}
              </p>
              <%!-- Per-item reveal, the SAME affordance the rail has. A real
                   focusable button, never a hover treatment: `@media (hover:
                   hover)` never matches on a touch device, so a hover-only
                   reveal would leave the drawer with no way to show one org at
                   all. Sized to the 44px touch floor. --%>
              <button
                :if={
                  @mask_names? and
                    not Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.revealed?(drawer_mask_ctx, section)
                }
                type="button"
                class="channel-section-reveal-button channel-section-reveal-button--touch"
                phx-click="reveal_section"
                phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                aria-label="Show this workspace name"
              >
                <span class="hero-eye size-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              </button>
              <%!-- Up/down move buttons (Stage 4 — WCAG 2.5.7 Dragging
                 Movements): the REQUIRED single-pointer alternative to the
                 long-press drag, not an optional nicety. They fire the SAME
                 `section_reordered {from, to}` event the drag sends — one
                 server path, two triggers. The event's semantics are "insert
                 `from` ABOVE `to`" (mirroring the drop indicator), which has
                 no direct "move below" form — so Down on section A is
                 expressed as "insert my NEXT sibling above me"
                 (from=next.id, to=this.id), which is the same swap. Boundary
                 buttons are disabled, not hidden, mirroring the desktop row
                 controls: focus can't land on a no-op that reads as broken.
                 Pinned/DMs render none of this (locked).

                 Stage 1 search guard rail: ALL reorder affordances vanish
                 while a search filter is active — a reorder computed against
                 a filtered subset would persist a wrong order. This gate is
                 also what keeps the neighbor-index math above safe. --%>
              <span
                :if={@sidebar_edit && @drawer_query == ""}
                class="channel-section-move-controls"
              >
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-section-move-button--touch"
                  phx-click="section_reordered"
                  phx-value-from={section.id}
                  phx-value-to={
                    section_index > 0 &&
                      Enum.at(@sidebar_sections, section_index - 1).section.id
                  }
                  disabled={section_index == 0}
                  aria-label={
                    "Move #{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(drawer_mask_ctx, section)} section up"
                  }
                  title="Move section up"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-up size-4"></span>
                </button>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-section-move-button--touch"
                  phx-click="section_reordered"
                  phx-value-from={
                    section_index < length(@sidebar_sections) - 1 &&
                      Enum.at(@sidebar_sections, section_index + 1).section.id
                  }
                  phx-value-to={section.id}
                  disabled={section_index == length(@sidebar_sections) - 1}
                  aria-label={
                    "Move #{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(drawer_mask_ctx, section)} section down"
                  }
                  title="Move section down"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-down size-4"></span>
                </button>
              </span>
              <%!-- Touch drag handle (Stage 3) — the ONLY drag origin: a touch
                 starting outside it scrolls the rail, never drags (Stage 4
                 checklist #6 verifies this). Edit-gated like the Stage 2 lock
                 affordances; locked sections render no handle at all.
                 `tabindex="-1"` because the keyboard/a11y reorder path is the
                 Stage 4 up/down buttons beside it, not this gesture
                 affordance. --%>
              <button
                :if={@sidebar_edit && @drawer_query == ""}
                type="button"
                class="channel-section-drag-handle channel-section-drag-handle--touch"
                aria-label={
                  "Reorder #{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label(drawer_mask_ctx, section)} section — touch and hold, then drag"
                }
                tabindex="-1"
              >
                ☰
              </button>
            </div>
            <%= cond do %>
              <% section_channels == [] -> %>
                <p class="px-4 py-2 text-sm text-base-content/50">
                  No channels yet — channels in this org appear here.
                </p>
              <% @sidebar_edit && @drawer_query == "" -> %>
                <%!-- EDIT-MODE rows (channel-row reorder Stage 1; revised in
                   Stage 2). Rows stop being navigation links — a mis-tap
                   would navigate + close the drawer, ejecting the user from
                   the mode. Every row shows its ▲▼ pair persistently, the
                   same convention as the section headers directly above them
                   (Marlowe a11y request 2026-07-09, reversing the July 6
                   select-to-reveal decision: controls that hide until touched
                   read as broken, and were reported as a bug twice in one
                   review). The unread badge yields its right-edge slot to the
                   reorder chrome (edit mode is a mode; counts are browse
                   chrome). Boundary ▲▼ are disabled, not hidden, matching
                   the section buttons. Reorder reuses the EXISTING
                   move_channel pipeline (per-user chat_channel_order pref) —
                   the same one desktop's row controls persist through. --%>
                <div
                  :for={{space, row_index} <- Enum.with_index(section_channels)}
                  data-channel-id={space.id}
                  data-section-id={section.id}
                  class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm"
                >
                  <span class="text-base-content/40 text-lg">#</span>
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">
                    {Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(drawer_mask_ctx, section, space.name)}
                  </span>
                  <span class="channel-row-move-controls--touch">
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="channel-row-move-button--touch"
                      phx-click="move_channel"
                      phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                      phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                      phx-value-direction="up"
                      disabled={row_index == 0}
                      aria-label={
                        "Move ##{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(drawer_mask_ctx, section, space.name)} up"
                      }
                      title="Move up"
                    >
                      <span class="hero-chevron-up size-4"></span>
                    </button>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="channel-row-move-button--touch"
                      phx-click="move_channel"
                      phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                      phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                      phx-value-direction="down"
                      disabled={row_index == length(section_channels) - 1}
                      aria-label={
                        "Move ##{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(drawer_mask_ctx, section, space.name)} down"
                      }
                      title="Move down"
                    >
                      <span class="hero-chevron-down size-4"></span>
                    </button>
                    <%!-- Touch drag handle (Stage 2) — the ONLY row-drag
                       origin; activates the slot Stage 1 held with an inert
                       placeholder. Lives INSIDE the controls cluster so the
                       row's gap-3 can't wedge 12px between ▼ and ☰ — that
                       offset broke column alignment with the section header
                       (design QA, 2026-07-09). `tabindex="-1"` because the
                       keyboard/a11y reorder path is the always-visible ▲▼
                       buttons beside it, not this gesture affordance
                       (WCAG 2.5.7 coupling, same as sections). --%>
                    <button
                      type="button"
                      class="channel-row-drag-handle"
                      aria-label={
                        "Reorder ##{Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(drawer_mask_ctx, section, space.name)} — touch and hold, then drag"
                      }
                      tabindex="-1"
                    >
                      ☰
                    </button>
                  </span>
                </div>
              <% true -> %>
                <%!-- Row wrapper (task 019fe998). NORMAL mode only: the
                     edit-mode branch above already carries its own persistent
                     ▲▼ + drag cluster, and the sheet deliberately offers no
                     Move — arrows are for repeated nudging inside an explicit
                     arranging mode, and reordering a list by opening a sheet
                     per step would be miserable. --%>
                <div
                  :for={space <- section_channels}
                  class="flex items-center"
                  data-role="drawer-row-wrap"
                  data-space-id={space.id}
                >
                  <.link
                    patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                    phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
                    class={[
                      "flex flex-1 min-w-0 items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
                      "hover:bg-base-200",
                      @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
                        "bg-base-200 text-primary font-semibold"
                    ]}
                  >
                    <span class="text-base-content/40 text-lg">#</span>
                    <span class="truncate flex-1">
                      {Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(
                        drawer_mask_ctx,
                        section,
                        space.name
                      )}
                    </span>
                    <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                      <span class="ml-1 flex-shrink-0 min-w-[1.125rem] h-[1.125rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.6rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center px-1 leading-none">
                        {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                      </span>
                    <% end %>
                  </.link>
                  <.row_actions_control
                    space_id={space.id}
                    name={
                      Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.channel_label(
                        drawer_mask_ctx,
                        section,
                        space.name
                      )
                    }
                  />
                </div>
            <% end %>
          </section>

          <%!-- Archived channels (task 019e95ea stage 2) — same collapsed
             group as the desktop rail, driven by the same @archived_channels
             / @archived_open assigns. Hidden while a search is active: the
             drawer_filter_* helpers only know the active sections, and
             archived rows shouldn't surface as phantom search results. --%>
          <section
            :if={@archived_channels != [] and @drawer_query == ""}
            data-section-reorderable="false"
            aria-label="Archived channels"
          >
            <button
              type="button"
              class="flex w-full items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-1 mt-2 text-left"
              phx-click="toggle_archived_section"
              aria-expanded={if @archived_open, do: "true", else: "false"}
              aria-controls="archived-channel-list-mobile"
            >
              <span class="hero-archive-box size-3.5 text-base-content/40"></span>
              <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                Archived
              </p>
              <span class="ml-auto text-base-content/40 text-xs">
                {if @archived_open, do: "▾", else: "▸"}
              </span>
            </button>
            <div :if={@archived_open} id="archived-channel-list-mobile">
              <.link
                :for={space <- @archived_channels}
                patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
                phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
                class={[
                  "flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
                  "text-base-content/50 hover:bg-base-200",
                  @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
                    "bg-base-200 font-semibold"
                ]}
              >
                <span class="hero-archive-box size-4 text-base-content/30"></span>
                <span class="truncate flex-1">{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}</span>
              </.link>
            </div>
          </section>

          <%!-- No-matches state (Stage 1) — ONLY for an active search that
             matched nothing; the account-empty state below stays reserved
             for a genuinely conversation-less account. The likeliest miss is
             searching a PERSON's name (that's the other search), so the dead
             end hands off to the new-conversation people picker rather than
             apologizing. --%>
          <div
            :if={
              @drawer_query != "" and
                drawer_no_matches?(
                  pinned_rail_entries(@channel_sections.pinned, @pinned_task_spaces),
                  @channel_sections,
                  @sidebar_sections,
                  @drawer_query,
                  @user_id,
                  drawer_mask_ctx
                )
            }
            class="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 px-6 py-10 text-center"
          >
            <span class="hero-magnifying-glass size-8 text-base-content/30" aria-hidden="true">
            </span>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium">No matches for “{@drawer_query}”</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">
              Check the spelling, or start a new conversation.
            </p>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-1">
              <button
                type="button"
                phx-click={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
                class="flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 px-4 rounded-lg bg-base-200 border border-base-content/10 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-base-300"
              >
                New conversation
              </button>
              <button
                type="button"
                phx-click="drawer_search_clear"
                class="flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 px-4 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-base-content/60 hover:text-base-content hover:bg-base-200"
              >
                Clear search
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%!-- Empty state per docs/design-system/03-voice.md §5.1 — mobile
             combined view (no channels AND no DMs). Chip event is a JS
             chain so opening the new-conversation flow also closes the
             mobile browser overlay. Suppressed while a search is active —
             the no-matches state above owns that case. --%>
          <.empty_state
            :if={@channels == [] and @dm_conversations == [] and @drawer_query == ""}
            variant={:conversational}
          >
            <:system_message>— no conversations yet —</:system_message>
            <:body>
              Start your first conversation. Pick a channel or DM someone in your space.
            </:body>
            <:chips
              label="+ Start your first conversation"
              event={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
            />
          </.empty_state>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <%!-- "+ New channel" — pinned overlay chrome, mirroring the desktop
           rail's foot button. Preserves the new-channel entry point that the
           old flat "Channels" header used to host; the JS chain closes the
           overlay as the create flow opens. --%>
      <%!-- pt-3 + .mobile-drawer-footer-safe (NOT py-3 + .safe-area-bottom):
           the safe-area utility REPLACES padding-bottom with the device
           inset, which is 0 on desktop — in a desktop PWA the window's
           rounded corners then clip the label (Marlowe, 2026-07-05). The
           footer class adds the inset ON TOP of the normal padding. --%>
      <button
        phx-click={JS.push("new_channel_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
        aria-label="New channel"
        class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 w-full border-t border-base-300 px-4 pt-3 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors mobile-drawer-footer-safe"
      >
        <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
        <span>New channel</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%!-- External mobile channel switcher (task 019f9257-a83e). The internal
       `#mobile-channel-browser` above is `!@external?`-gated because its
       sectioned org-tree browser, new-channel affordance and scope-pills are
       all internal-discovery chrome. External users get this FLAT parallel:
       the same `fixed inset-0 z-40 lg:hidden` shell + `drawer_search` +
       `DrawerSearchFocus` hook, but a single flat `@channels ++
       @dm_conversations` list (the exact set the external rail renders), plus
       the Fabrikam brand / identity / logout that the chrome-less `:external`
       layout (layouts.ex) has nowhere else to hang on mobile. Opened by the
       pills-strip search button (`toggle_mobile_browser`); on the no-space
       landing it is shown by default — the list IS the landing (iOS-Messages
       model, Saru direction). Semantic tokens only; safe-area utilities reused
       from the internal overlay. --%>
  <% external_switcher_spaces = @channels ++ @dm_conversations %>
  <%= if @external? and !@embedded and (@mobile_browser_open or is_nil(@active_space)) do %>
    <div
      id="external-mobile-switcher"
      data-role="external-mobile-switcher"
      class="fixed inset-0 z-40 flex flex-col bg-base-100 lg:hidden safe-area-x"
    >
      <header class="flex-shrink-0 border-b border-base-300 safe-area-top">
        <div class="flex h-12 items-center justify-between px-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0" data-role="brand-chip">
            <img src={~p"/images/logo.svg"} alt="Fabrikam" class="size-6 flex-shrink-0" />
            <span class="truncate text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-base-content">
              Fabrikam
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1">
            <a
              href={~p"/auth/logout"}
              class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm btn-square"
              aria-label="Log out"
              data-role="external-logout"
            >
              <span class="hero-arrow-right-start-on-rectangle size-5"></span>
            </a>
            <%!-- No close control on the landing (is_nil(@active_space)) — the
                 switcher IS the screen there, nothing to reveal behind it. --%>
            <button
              :if={@active_space}
              phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
              class="flex items-center justify-center size-10 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content"
              aria-label="Close"
            >
              <span class="hero-x-mark size-5"></span>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          :if={@external_user}
          class="flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-base-300 px-4 py-2"
          data-role="external-identity"
        >
          <.human_avatar
            name={@external_user.name || @external_user.email || "You"}
            avatar_url={@external_user.avatar_url}
            seed={@external_user.oidc_sub || @external_user.email || @external_user.id}
            size="sm"
            class="flex-shrink-0"
          />
          <span class="truncate text-sm text-base-content">
            {@external_user.name || @external_user.email}
          </span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <%!-- Pinned search row — reuses the internal drawer's events + hook so
           iOS focus/zoom behaviour is identical (h-11 >=44px target, text-base
           blocks auto-zoom). Stable `drawer-search-input` id is shared with the
           internal overlay, which is `!@external?`-gated so only one is ever in
           the DOM. --%>
      <div class="flex-shrink-0 px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-300" role="search">
        <form class="relative" phx-change="drawer_search" phx-submit="drawer_search">
          <span
            class="hero-magnifying-glass absolute left-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 size-4 text-base-content/40"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
          </span>
          <input
            id="drawer-search-input"
            type="search"
            name="value"
            value={@drawer_query}
            phx-hook="DrawerSearchFocus"
            data-search-intent={to_string(@drawer_search_intent)}
            phx-debounce="150"
            placeholder="Find a conversation"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocorrect="off"
            autocapitalize="none"
            spellcheck="false"
            enterkeyhint="go"
            aria-label="Find a conversation"
            class="w-full h-11 rounded-lg bg-base-200 border border-base-content/10 pl-9 pr-11 text-base placeholder:text-base-content/40 focus:border-primary focus:outline-none"
          />
          <button
            :if={@drawer_query != ""}
            type="button"
            phx-click="drawer_search_clear"
            class="absolute right-0 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center justify-center min-h-11 min-w-11 text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content"
            aria-label="Clear search"
          >
            <span class="hero-x-mark size-4"></span>
          </button>
        </form>
      </div>

      <% external_switcher_filtered =
        drawer_filter_external_spaces(external_switcher_spaces, @drawer_query, @user_id) %>
      <nav class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2" aria-label="Your conversations">
        <%= if external_switcher_spaces == [] do %>
          <%!-- Calm zero-allowlist empty state — mirrors the external rail's
               `external-empty`. NEVER an internal "browse channels" hint. --%>
          <div
            class="flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 text-center"
            data-role="external-empty"
          >
            <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-8 text-base-content/30"></span>
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70">Nothing here yet</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50">
              Your conversations will appear here.
            </p>
          </div>
        <% else %>
          <%= if external_switcher_filtered == [] do %>
            <p class="px-4 py-6 text-center text-sm text-base-content/50">No matches</p>
          <% else %>
            <.link
              :for={space <- external_switcher_filtered}
              patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
              class={[
                "channel-row",
                @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
              ]}
            >
              <span :if={space.kind == "channel"} class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
              <span class="truncate flex-1">
                {if space.kind == "channel",
                  do: masked_space_name(assigns, space.name),
                  else: sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}
              </span>
              <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                  {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                </span>
              <% end %>
            </.link>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </nav>

      <%!-- DM picker foot — the ONE discovery affordance external users keep
           (filtered to allowlisted humans server-side). Closes the switcher as
           the create flow opens. `mobile-drawer-footer-safe` adds the
           home-indicator inset ON TOP of the normal padding. --%>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
        aria-label="New conversation"
        data-role="external-new-conversation"
        class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 w-full border-t border-base-300 px-4 pt-3 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors mobile-drawer-footer-safe"
      >
        <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
        <span>New conversation</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex flex-1 overflow-hidden min-w-0 min-h-0">
    <div
      id="chat-drop-zone"
      phx-hook="DragDropUpload"
      class="flex flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden min-w-0 min-h-0"
    >
      <header
        :if={@active_space && !@embedded}
        class="flex h-12 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b border-base-content/10 px-5"
      >
        <%!-- Screen-share masking (task 01a00c66 stage 5). The open channel's
             own name sits in this header at the top of the screen; masking the
             rail row for `#wayne-tech` and leaving the header spelling it out is
             the same leak with an extra step. `space_label/3` looks the name up
             across the whole rail because this header has no section in hand.
             Applied to BOTH breakpoint branches below — the mobile and desktop
             titles are separate nodes, and a mask applied to one of them is the
             shape of bug this stage exists to find. --%>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden">
          <%!-- Mobile: static channel name. Channel switching now happens via the
               pills strip below the header (Refined Option A — Marlowe approval
               2026-05-10). The previous tap-channel-name-to-open-browser flow
               was confusing with the shell's hamburger menu — both opened
               drawers, so users could tap one when they meant the other. The
               pills strip makes channel switching 1-tap and removes the
               dual-affordance ambiguity. The overflow magnifying-glass icon at
               the right of the strip still opens the full channel browser
               (this template's @mobile_browser_open overlay) for the long-tail
               jump-to-channel case. --%>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden lg:hidden">
            <span :if={@active_space.kind == "channel"} class="text-base-content/50">#</span>
            <span class="truncate font-semibold">
              {space_header_name(
                @active_space,
                @space_participants,
                @user_id,
                space_mask(assigns)
              )}
            </span>
            <%!-- Compact scope-pill on the mobile chat header (chat sidebar
                 mobile Stage 2, Decision #6). Mirrors the desktop header pill
                 (the `hidden lg:flex` block just below) but uses the foundation
                 task's `:compact` size variant for the tight mobile bar. Only
                 rendered for channels — `@active_space_scope` is nil for
                 DMs/groups (no org-scope), so the pill is suppressed there. The
                 `.chat-header-scope-pill-mobile` wrapper enlarges the compact
                 pill's tap target to >=44x44px (app.css): the shared
                 `.scope-pill-hit-expand` overlay only clears the 24px WCAG floor
                 and would be clipped by this row's overflow-hidden. --%>
            <% mobile_header_scope = !@external? && @active_space_scope %>
            <span
              :if={mobile_header_scope}
              class="chat-header-scope-pill-mobile flex-shrink-0"
            >
              <%!-- Masked like the rail (task 01a00c66 stage 3): this pill sits
                   in the chat header at the top of the phone screen, which is
                   the MOST visible surface in a mirrored window. The label
                   override reaches the pill's `aria-label` too. --%>
              <.scope_pill
                scope={mobile_header_scope}
                size={:compact}
                clickable={true}
                active={@scope_filter == mobile_header_scope}
                label={
                  @mask_names? &&
                    Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label_for_bucket(
                      Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.context(
                        @sidebar_sections,
                        @mask_names?,
                        @revealed_section_ids
                      ),
                      @sidebar_sections,
                      PlatformWeb.ChatLive.bucket_for_scope(mobile_header_scope)
                    )
                }
              />
            </span>
          </div>
          <%!-- Desktop: static title --%>
          <span class="hidden lg:flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden">
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "channel"}
              class="text-base-content/50 text-lg font-bold"
            >
              #
            </span>
            <span class="truncate font-bold text-base">
              {space_header_name(
                @active_space,
                @space_participants,
                @user_id,
                space_mask(assigns)
              )}
            </span>
            <%!-- Prominent chat-header scope-pill (chat plan v2 Stage 4).
                 Only rendered for channels (DMs/groups have no scope). The
                 wrapper class drives the larger-size visual variant; the
                 inner pill remains clickable and pushes the `scope_filter`
                 event with the channel's scope. Active state is implied
                 from `@scope_filter` so a clicked-again pill reads as the
                 currently-selected filter. --%>
            <% header_scope = !@external? && @active_space_scope %>
            <span :if={header_scope} class="chat-header-scope-pill">
              <.scope_pill
                scope={header_scope}
                clickable={true}
                active={@scope_filter == header_scope}
                label={
                  @mask_names? &&
                    Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.label_for_bucket(
                      Platform.Chat.SidebarMask.context(
                        @sidebar_sections,
                        @mask_names?,
                        @revealed_section_ids
                      ),
                      @sidebar_sections,
                      PlatformWeb.ChatLive.bucket_for_scope(header_scope)
                    )
                }
              />
            </span>
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "channel" && @active_space.topic}
              class="truncate text-xs text-base-content/40"
            >
              — {@active_space.topic}
            </span>
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "group"}
              class="text-xs text-base-content/40"
            >
              — {length(@space_participants)} members
            </span>
          </span>

          <%!-- Promote to channel button for groups --%>
          <form
            :if={@active_space.kind == "group" && !@active_space.is_direct}
            id="promote-to-channel-form"
            phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
            phx-submit="promote_to_channel"
            class="hidden lg:flex items-center gap-1 ml-2"
          >
            <input
              name="name"
              type="text"
              aria-label="Channel name"
              placeholder="Channel name…"
              class="input input-bordered input-xs w-32"
              required
            />
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost">
              Convert to Channel
            </button>
          </form>
        </div>

        <%!-- Join Meeting button.

           `!@external?` (task 019fb955-f8b1 stage 5): the LiveKit room is
           keyed off the space, so this button offered an external user in
           a meeting's bound chat space the very join `MeetingHooks`
           refuses server-side as of stage 4 — "chat is chat only". THE
           SERVER REFUSAL IS THE GATE; this is cosmetics over it. Removing
           the condition here re-exposes a dead button, not a hole. A
           button that does nothing when clicked is quiet degradation, and
           that is the whole reason this line exists. --%>
        <button
          :if={@meetings_enabled && !@in_meeting && !@external?}
          phx-click="meeting_join"
          class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium text-base-content/60 hover:text-primary hover:bg-primary/10 transition-colors"
          title="Start or join a meeting in this space"
        >
          <span class="hero-video-camera size-4"></span>
          <span class="hidden md:inline">Meet</span>
        </button>

        <div class="flex flex-shrink-0 items-center gap-3 text-xs text-base-content/50">
          <.form
            for={@search_form}
            id="chat-search-form"
            phx-change="search_submit"
            phx-submit="search_submit"
            class="hidden md:block"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <.input
                field={@search_form[:query]}
                type="text"
                aria-label="Search messages in this space"
                placeholder="Search messages…"
                autocomplete="off"
                phx-debounce="250"
                class="input input-sm w-64 text-sm"
              />

              <button
                :if={present?(@search_query)}
                type="button"
                phx-click="search_clear"
                class="rounded px-2 py-1 text-xs hover:bg-base-300"
              >
                Clear
              </button>
            </div>
          </.form>

          <button
            :if={@canvases != []}
            phx-click="canvas_panel_toggle"
            class={[
              "flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300",
              @show_canvases && "!bg-base-300 !text-primary"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="hero-puzzle-piece size-4"></span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">{length(@canvases)}</span>
          </button>

          <button
            :if={@pins != []}
            phx-click="pin_panel_toggle"
            class={[
              "flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300",
              @show_pins && "!bg-base-300 !text-primary"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="hero-bookmark-solid size-4"></span>
            <span>{length(@pins)} pinned</span>
          </button>

          <%!-- Agent eye — the ONE control for the agent mutex (task 019f9790
               stage 4). It replaces three competing header controls that used
               to sit here: the "Talking to {name}" pill with its own x-mark
               sub-button, the dimmed "{primary} listening" hint, and the
               `watch_enabled` toggle. Those three could disagree with each
               other and none of them was the thing that actually routes
               messages. This button IS the mutex (`ActiveAgentStore`):

                 open   — a mutex is held; the next message goes to that agent.
                          Click closes it (`active_agent_clear`).
                 closed — no mutex, but `ActiveAgentHooks.resolve_armable/2`
                          found a defensible target. Click opens it
                          (`active_agent_arm`).
                 inert  — no mutex and no defensible target (several agents, no
                          history). Rendered `disabled` rather than hidden so
                          the header never reflows as agents join or leave.

               DM spaces render nothing: `attention_router.ex:343` makes DMs
               unconditionally `:directed`, so there is nothing here to toggle
               and offering the control would be a lie.

               `data-role` / `data-eye-state` exist so tests assert on state
               rather than on Tailwind classes. `min-h-11 min-w-11` gives the
               iOS-HIG 44px touch target on mobile (measured: 20px tall without
               it); released at `md` so the desktop hover surface still matches
               the sibling pin/settings buttons. --%>
          <% eye_state =
            cond do
              @active_agent_participant_id != nil -> "open"
              @active_agent_armable_id != nil -> "closed"
              true -> "inert"
            end %>
          <button
            :if={
              (@agent_presence[:joined?] || @has_agent_participant) && @active_space.kind != "dm"
            }
            data-role="agent-eye"
            data-eye-state={eye_state}
            disabled={eye_state == "inert"}
            phx-click={
              case eye_state do
                "open" -> "active_agent_clear"
                "closed" -> "active_agent_arm"
                _inert -> nil
              end
            }
            class={[
              "flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs transition-colors md:min-h-0 md:min-w-0",
              eye_state == "open" && "text-success hover:bg-base-300",
              eye_state == "closed" &&
                "text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content hover:bg-base-300",
              eye_state == "inert" && "text-base-content/50 opacity-50"
            ]}
            title={
              case eye_state do
                "open" ->
                  "Your next message goes to #{@active_agent_name || "Agent"} — click to talk to people only"

                "closed" ->
                  "Click to resume with #{@active_agent_armable_name || "the agent"}"

                _inert ->
                  "No agent is listening — @mention an agent to open the eye"
              end
            }
          >
            <span class={[
              "size-4",
              if(eye_state == "open", do: "hero-eye", else: "hero-eye-slash")
            ]}>
            </span>
            <span :if={eye_state == "open"} class="hidden md:inline">
              {@active_agent_name || "Agent"}
            </span>
          </button>

          <button
            phx-click="settings_open"
            class="flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300"
            title="Space settings"
          >
            <span class="hero-cog-6-tooth size-4"></span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">settings</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </header>

      <%!-- Mobile Pinned strip (task 019f923b Stage 1). `lg:hidden` mirrors the
           `hidden lg:flex` gate on <aside id="chat-sidebar">: without this
           strip, pinned spaces (both task-exec pins from `@pinned_task_spaces`
           and channel pins from `@channel_sections.pinned`) are unreachable
           on <lg viewports because the desktop rail is hidden.

           Renders horizontally-scrollable chips that mirror the desktop
           rail's mental model — `hero-clipboard-document-list-mini` for
           task-exec pins and, for pinned conversations, the desktop Pinned
           block's row identity: a bare name for a person, `#` for a channel.
           Chips carry the unread badge from `unread_label/1` when the space
           has unread messages, using the same visual language as the
           channel-pills strip immediately below.

           Auto-hides when BOTH lists are empty — no permanent header. The
           `:if` OR-guard means a user with only pinned tasks (or only pinned
           channels, once channel-pinning ships) still gets the strip; the
           strip only disappears when the user has no pins at all.

           Sits ABOVE the channel-pills strip so pinned spaces are the first
           navigation surface a user sees when landing in a channel on mobile.
           Pinned channels intentionally re-appear in the channel-pills strip
           below (via `Sidebar.flatten_sections/1`) — that duplication is
           deliberate visual emphasis on pinned items, not a bug to
           deduplicate.

           Conversation pinning IS wired as of task 019fd80f stage 2: every
           `channel_sections/4` call site passes the user's real pin list, so
           the conversation-chip branch below is live. It was dead before
           that, which is why it rendered `{space.name}` for every kind and
           produced a blank chip for a pinned DM. Render coverage for both
           kinds is in `chat_live_pinned_block_test.exs`. --%>
      <nav
        :if={
          @active_space && !@embedded &&
            (@pinned_task_spaces != [] || @channel_sections.pinned != [])
        }
        class="lg:hidden flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/40"
        style="scrollbar-width: none; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;"
        aria-label="Pinned"
        data-role="mobile-pinned-strip"
      >
        <.link
          :for={space <- @pinned_task_spaces}
          patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
          data-role="mobile-pinned-task-chip"
          data-space-id={space.id}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0",
            if(@active_space.id == space.id,
              do: "bg-primary text-primary-content",
              else: "bg-base-100 text-base-content/80 border border-base-content/10"
            )
          ]}
        >
          <%!-- The task marker, and the SAME glyph the two rail surfaces use
               for a task row. It was `hero-map-pin-mini` here until
               2026-08-11: one concept carried two glyphs depending on which
               surface a person happened to be looking at, and the glyph is
               the only thing distinguishing the three kinds, so the two had
               to converge. `hero-clipboard-document-list-mini` is what Saru's
               design canvas for 019feec6-73d9 specifies. --%>
          <span class={[
            "hero-clipboard-document-list-mini size-3.5",
            if(@active_space.id == space.id,
              do: "text-primary-content/80",
              else: "text-base-content/40"
            )
          ]}>
          </span>
          <span class="truncate max-w-[10rem]">
            {Platform.Tasks.ChatPins.display_name_for_space(space)}
          </span>
          <span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >
            {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
          </span>
        </.link>
        <.link
          :for={space <- @channel_sections.pinned}
          patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
          data-role="mobile-pinned-channel-chip"
          data-space-id={space.id}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0",
            if(@active_space.id == space.id,
              do: "bg-primary text-primary-content",
              else: "bg-base-100 text-base-content/80 border border-base-content/10"
            )
          ]}
        >
          <%!-- Same identity rule as the two rail surfaces: `#` plus a name
               for a channel, a bare name for a person.

               No `hero-bookmark-solid`: every chip in this strip is a pin, so
               a pin marker on all of them never varied and carried nothing.
               The task chips above carry `hero-clipboard-document-list-mini`,
               which does vary, since it separates a task from a
               conversation — and it is the same glyph the rail uses, so one
               concept has one mark on every surface.

               No empty indent slot on the person chips either, unlike the two
               rail surfaces. Chips sit in a horizontal scroller, so there is
               no name column to keep straight, and a blank 20px inside a pill
               would read as broken padding rather than as an absent glyph. --%>
          <%= if space.kind in ["dm", "group"] do %>
            <span class="truncate max-w-[10rem]">{sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}</span>
          <% else %>
            <span
              class={[
                "shrink-0",
                if(@active_space.id == space.id,
                  do: "text-primary-content/80",
                  else: "text-base-content/40"
                )
              ]}
              data-role="pinned-row-hash"
            >
              #
            </span>
            <span class="truncate max-w-[10rem]">{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}</span>
          <% end %>
          <span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >
            {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
          </span>
        </.link>
      </nav>

      <%!-- Mobile-only channel pills strip — Refined Option A nav (Marlowe approval 2026-05-10).
           Replaces the previous tap-channel-name-to-open-browser flow. Horizontally
           scrollable pills with the active channel highlighted; the magnifying-glass
           icon at the LEFT opens the @mobile_browser_open drawer (search + full
           channel/DM list). 1-tap switching for the pills shown; 2-tap
           (magnifying glass → search) for the long tail.

           ORDERING CONTRACT (Marlowe decision 2026-07-05, this task's Stage 3):
           pills render `Sidebar.flatten_sections(@sidebar_sections)` — the user's
           curated drawer arrangement flattened left-to-right — NOT the raw
           @channels list. Consequences, both deliberate: (1) dragging sections
           in the drawer reorders the pills identically (one mental model,
           stable muscle memory — the unread badge signals activity without
           moving pills); (2) hidden channels/sections are absent here too —
           hidden means hidden everywhere. Historical note: the raw @channels
           order this replaced was channel CREATION order (Chat.list_spaces
           sorts by inserted_at), not "alphabetical" as previously claimed
           here. The old Stage 1B localStorage-pinning idea is superseded by
           the server-side section order. --%>
      <nav
        :if={@active_space && !@embedded}
        class="lg:hidden flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-content/10"
        style="scrollbar-width: none; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;"
        aria-label="Channel switcher"
      >
        <%!-- Search/jump button anchored at the LEFT of the pills strip
             (Rowan request, Marlowe approval 2026-05-11). Sticks to the left
             edge so it stays in reach even as the channel pills overflow
             horizontally and scroll. phx-value-intent="search" (Stage 2):
             this entry declares search intent, so the drawer opens with the
             search field focused — other openers get a browse-first drawer. --%>
        <button
          phx-click="toggle_mobile_browser"
          phx-value-intent="search"
          class="flex items-center justify-center w-9 h-9 rounded-full shrink-0 bg-base-200 border border-base-content/10 text-base-content/50 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors sticky left-0 z-10"
          aria-label="Search channels and direct messages"
          title="Search channels and DMs"
        >
          <span class="hero-magnifying-glass size-4"></span>
        </button>

        <%!-- Channel pill source (task 019f9257-a83e): internal users get their
             curated flattened section order; external users have no
             `@sidebar_sections` (that resolver-driven org tree is empty for
             them), so their pills come from the flat granted-channel list
             `@channels` — the same set the external rail + switcher render.
             Without this branch the external pills strip showed only DMs and
             none of the user's channels. --%>
        <% switcher_channel_pills =
          if @external?, do: @channels, else: Sidebar.flatten_sections(@sidebar_sections) %>
        <.link
          :for={space <- switcher_channel_pills}
          patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0 transition-all",
            "active:scale-[0.97] ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]",
            if @active_space.id == space.id do
              "bg-primary text-primary-content shadow-[0_0_16px_oklch(0.78_0.14_207_/_0.18)]"
            else
              "bg-base-200 text-base-content/70 border border-base-content/10 hover:bg-base-300"
            end
          ]}
        >
          <span class={[
            if(@active_space.id == space.id,
              do: "text-primary-content/80",
              else: "text-base-content/40"
            )
          ]}>#</span>{masked_space_name(assigns, space.name)}<span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >{unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}</span>
        </.link>

        <%!-- DM pills (after channels, no divider for now to keep mobile compact) --%>
        <.link
          :for={space <- @dm_conversations}
          patch={~p"/chat/#{space_nav_target(space)}"}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0 transition-all",
            "active:scale-[0.97] ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]",
            if @active_space.id == space.id do
              "bg-primary text-primary-content shadow-[0_0_16px_oklch(0.78_0.14_207_/_0.18)]"
            else
              "bg-base-200 text-base-content/70 border border-base-content/10 hover:bg-base-300"
            end
          ]}
        >
          {sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}<span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >{unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}</span>
        </.link>
      </nav>

      <div
        :if={present?(@search_query)}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-3"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              Search Results
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
              “{@search_query}” · {length(@search_results)} match{if length(@search_results) == 1,
                do: "",
                else: "es"}
            </p>
          </div>

          <button phx-click="search_clear" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs">
            Clear
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-3 space-y-2">
          <button
            :for={result <- @search_results}
            type="button"
            phx-click="search_open_result"
            phx-value-message-id={result.id}
            class="block w-full rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3 py-2 text-left transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-base-100/80"
          >
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              <span>{PresenceHooks.sender_name(@participants_map, result.participant_id)}</span>
              <.local_time
                id={"search-time-#{result.id}"}
                timestamp={result.inserted_at}
              />
              <span
                :if={is_binary(result.thread_id)}
                class="rounded-full bg-base-300 px-2 py-0.5 normal-case tracking-normal text-[10px]"
              >
                Thread
              </span>
              <span
                :if={result.search_rank}
                class="font-mono normal-case tracking-normal text-[10px] text-base-content/40"
              >
                rank {Float.round(result.search_rank, 3)}
              </span>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content">
              {search_headline(result)}
            </p>
          </button>

          <%!-- Empty state per docs/design-system/03-voice.md §5.5 — search
               no-results uses :standard with the magnifying-glass icon. --%>
          <.empty_state
            :if={@search_results == [] and present?(@search_query)}
            variant={:standard}
            icon_name="hero-magnifying-glass"
          >
            <:title>No matches</:title>
            <:body>No messages match "{@search_query}".</:body>
            <:actions>
              <button
                type="button"
                phx-click="search_clear"
                class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm w-full"
              >
                Clear search
              </button>
            </:actions>
          </.empty_state>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        :if={@show_pins && @pins != []}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-2"
      >
        <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
          Pinned Messages
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 max-h-40 overflow-y-auto">
          <div
            :for={pin <- @pins}
            class="flex items-center justify-between rounded bg-base-100 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm"
          >
            <span class="truncate text-base-content/70 text-xs">
              <span class="hero-bookmark-solid size-3 inline-block align-text-bottom"></span>
              pinned message
              <span class="font-mono text-base-content/40 text-[10px]">
                {String.slice(pin.message_id, 0, 8)}…
              </span>
            </span>
            <button
              :if={@active_space && is_nil(@active_space.archived_at)}
              phx-click="pin_toggle"
              phx-value-message-id={pin.message_id}
              phx-value-space-id={pin.space_id}
              class="ml-2 text-xs text-base-content/40 hover:text-error"
            >
              Unpin
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        :if={@show_canvases}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-3"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-3 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_320px]">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              Live Canvases
            </p>

            <button
              :for={canvas <- @canvases}
              type="button"
              phx-click="canvas_open"
              phx-value-canvas-id={canvas.id}
              class={[
                "flex w-full items-center justify-between rounded-xl border px-3 py-2 text-left transition-colors",
                "border-base-300 bg-base-100 hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-base-100/80",
                @active_canvas && @active_canvas.id == canvas.id && "border-primary bg-primary/5"
              ]}
            >
              <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-base-content">
                  {canvas.title || CanvasHooks.humanize_kind(canvas)}
                </p>
                <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                  {CanvasHooks.humanize_kind(canvas)}
                </p>
              </div>

              <span class="ml-3 rounded-full bg-base-300 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-base-content/60">
                Open
              </span>
            </button>

            <div
              :if={@canvases == []}
              class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3 py-4 text-sm text-base-content/50"
            >
              No canvases yet. Create one to collaborate live in this channel.
            </div>
          </div>

          <.form
            for={@new_canvas_form}
            id="new-canvas-form"
            phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
            phx-submit="canvas_create"
            class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-4"
          >
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-base-content">New canvas</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50">
                Creates a canvas and posts a linked canvas message.
              </p>
            </div>

            <.input
              field={@new_canvas_form[:title]}
              label="Title"
              placeholder="Sprint planning board"
            />

            <button
              type="submit"
              class="btn btn-neutral w-full"
              disabled={is_nil(@current_participant)}
            >
              Create canvas
            </button>
          </.form>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="inline-focus-listener" phx-hook="InlineFocus" class="hidden"></div>
      <%!-- min-h-0 is the load-bearing class here: without it, flex items
           default to `min-height: auto` which means the message list
           refuses to shrink below its intrinsic content height. With 80+
           messages that intrinsic height blows past the viewport and
           pushes the composer + bottom-tab nav off-screen on iOS Safari /
           PWA standalone. overscroll-contain stops rubber-band gestures
           from reaching the document scroller (defence-in-depth: app.css
           already has `overscroll-behavior: none` on body, but iOS WebKit
           respects the per-scroller setting more reliably than the
           ancestor chain). --%>
      <%!-- Outer scroll wrapper for infinite scroll (task 019e18fc Stage
           3). The sentinels live inside this wrapper as siblings of
           #message-list — that way they're inside the scroll viewport
           and the InfiniteScroll IntersectionObserver fires when the
           user scrolls them into view. #message-list itself becomes a
           non-scrolling flex column inside the wrapper. Overflow +
           overscroll moved from #message-list to here. --%>
      <%!-- Archived read-only banner (task 019e95ea stage 2). Sits as a
           flex-shrink-0 sibling above the message scroller. The Unarchive
           button is gated on @can_unarchive? (computed server-side when
           :active_space is assigned) — affordance only, the context layer
           re-authorizes.

           Stage 4: when a deletion is scheduled the banner shows the purge
           date instead, with a Cancel button for Fabrikam admins only
           (@can_cancel_deletion?). Unarchive is hidden while deletion is
           pending — cancel first, then unarchive. Deletion-flagged channels
           are excluded from the sidebar's Archived section, so this banner
           is reached via direct URL; that's expected. --%>
      <div
        :if={@active_space && @active_space.archived_at}
        id="archived-banner"
        role="status"
        class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 px-5 py-2.5"
      >
        <%= if @active_space.deletion_scheduled_at do %>
          <span class="hero-trash size-4 flex-shrink-0 text-error"></span>
          <p class="flex-1 text-sm text-base-content/70">
            This channel is scheduled for permanent deletion on {Calendar.strftime(
              DateTime.add(
                @active_space.deletion_scheduled_at,
                Chat.space_retention_days(),
                :day
              ),
              "%B %-d, %Y"
            )} — it's read-only until then.
          </p>
          <button
            :if={@can_cancel_deletion?}
            type="button"
            phx-click="cancel_space_deletion"
            class="btn btn-outline btn-xs"
          >
            Cancel deletion
          </button>
        <% else %>
          <span class="hero-archive-box size-4 flex-shrink-0 text-base-content/60"></span>
          <p class="flex-1 text-sm text-base-content/70">
            This channel was archived on {Calendar.strftime(
              @active_space.archived_at,
              "%B %-d, %Y"
            )} — it's a read-only snapshot.
          </p>
          <button
            :if={@can_unarchive?}
            type="button"
            phx-click="unarchive_space"
            class="btn btn-outline btn-xs"
          >
            Unarchive
          </button>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div
        id="chat-message-scroller"
        data-scroll-container
        class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden overscroll-contain bg-base-100 [overflow-anchor:none]"
      >
        <%!-- Top sentinel: fires `load_older_messages` when visible AND
             :has_more_older is true. --%>
        <div
          :if={@has_more_older}
          id="chat-scroll-sentinel-top"
          phx-hook="InfiniteScroll"
          data-direction="older"
          data-loading={if @loading_older, do: "true"}
          class="flex justify-center py-2 text-xs text-base-content/40"
        >
          <span :if={@loading_older} class="hero-arrow-path size-3 animate-spin"></span>
          <span :if={!@loading_older}>Loading older messages…</span>
        </div>

        <div
          id="message-list"
          class="px-5 py-4 flex flex-col space-y-1"
          phx-update="stream"
          phx-hook="ScrollToBottom"
          data-anchor-message-id={@anchor_message_id}
        >
          <.chat_message
            :for={{dom_id, msg} <- @streams.messages}
            :if={is_nil(msg.deleted_at)}
            dom_id={dom_id}
            msg={msg}
            current_participant={@current_participant}
            agent_participant_ids={@agent_participant_ids}
            agent_colors_map={@agent_colors_map}
            participants_map={@participants_map}
            quick_emojis={@quick_emojis}
            pinned_message_ids={@pinned_message_ids}
            highlighted_message_id={@highlighted_message_id}
            canvases_by_id={@canvases_by_id}
            attachments_map={@attachments_map}
            thread_previews={@thread_previews}
            expanded_threads={@expanded_threads}
            inline_thread_messages={@inline_thread_messages}
            mention_suggestions={@mention_suggestions}
            mention_source={@mention_source}
            editing_message_id={@editing_message_id}
            read_only={@active_space != nil && @active_space.archived_at != nil}
          />
        </div>

        <%!-- Bottom sentinel: fires `load_newer_messages` when visible AND
             :newest_evicted? is true. Only renders after the live tail
             has been evicted by a prepend (Stage 2's prune logic). --%>
        <div
          :if={@newest_evicted?}
          id="chat-scroll-sentinel-bottom"
          phx-hook="InfiniteScroll"
          data-direction="newer"
          data-loading={if @loading_newer, do: "true"}
          class="flex justify-center py-2 text-xs text-base-content/40"
        >
          <span :if={@loading_newer} class="hero-arrow-path size-3 animate-spin"></span>
          <span :if={!@loading_newer}>Loading newer messages…</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%!-- Streaming reply bubbles --%>
      <div
        :for={{chunk_id, entry} <- @streaming_replies}
        :if={entry.text != nil and entry.text != ""}
        id={"streaming-#{chunk_id}"}
        class="flex-shrink-0 px-5 pb-2 msg-agent"
        style={
          "--agent-accent: #{Map.get(@agent_colors_map, entry.participant_id, Platform.Agents.ColorPalette.default_accent())};"
        }
      >
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <%!-- The face shown WHILE the agent is typing. It has to be the same
               avatar the settled message row draws, or the image would pop in
               only once the stream finishes and read as a rendering bug. --%>
          <.agent_avatar
            name={PresenceHooks.sender_name(@participants_map, entry.participant_id)}
            avatar_url={PresenceHooks.sender_avatar_url(@participants_map, entry.participant_id)}
            size="sm"
            class="msg-agent-avatar"
          />
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="text-xs font-medium mb-0.5 msg-agent-name">
              {PresenceHooks.sender_name(@participants_map, entry.participant_id)}
            </div>
            <div
              class="text-sm text-base-content/80 border-l-2 pl-3"
              style="border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--agent-accent, oklch(82% 0.12 207)) 30%, transparent);"
            >
              {entry.text}<span
                class="inline-block w-1.5 h-4 animate-pulse ml-0.5 align-middle rounded-sm"
                style="background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--agent-accent, oklch(82% 0.12 207)) 50%, transparent);"
              ></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%!-- Typing indicator --%>
      <div
        :if={not MapSet.equal?(@agent_typing_pids, MapSet.new()) and @streaming_replies == %{}}
        class="flex-shrink-0 px-5 pb-1 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-base-content/50"
      >
        <span class="flex gap-0.5 items-center">
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 0ms"
          >
          </span>
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 150ms"
          >
          </span>
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 300ms"
          >
          </span>
        </span>
        <span>
          {PresenceHooks.thinking_label(@agent_typing_pids, @participants_map)} is thinking…
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex-shrink-0 compose-input-area safe-area-bottom">
        <%!-- Composer is structurally absent on archived spaces (task
             019e95ea stage 2) — hiding is affordance; the context layer
             rejects the writes regardless. --%>
        <.form
          :if={@active_space && is_nil(@active_space.archived_at)}
          for={@compose_form}
          id="compose-form"
          phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
          phx-submit="send_message"
          phx-change="compose_changed"
          class="flex flex-col gap-2"
        >
          <%!-- @mention autocomplete dropdown --%>
          <div
            :if={@mention_suggestions != [] && @mention_source == "compose-form"}
            class="relative"
          >
            <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 z-50 w-64 rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
              <div class="py-1">
                <button
                  :for={{suggestion, idx} <- Enum.with_index(@mention_suggestions)}
                  type="button"
                  data-mention-suggestion={if idx == 0, do: "first"}
                  phx-click={
                    JS.dispatch("chat:insert-mention",
                      to: "##{@compose_form[:text].id}",
                      detail: %{name: suggestion.name}
                    )
                  }
                  class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-base-200 text-left transition-colors"
                >
                  <%= cond do %>
                    <% suggestion.participant_type == "broadcast" -> %>
                      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-warning/15 text-warning flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
                        <span class="hero-megaphone size-4"></span>
                      </div>
                    <% suggestion.participant_type == "agent" -> %>
                      <%!-- The human branch below already showed a stored photo
                           here; the agent branch drew a letter, so picking who
                           to @mention showed faces for people and initials for
                           agents. `suggestion.avatar_url` was in hand the whole
                           time — the identity map fills it for agents too. --%>
                      <.agent_avatar
                        name={suggestion.name}
                        avatar_url={suggestion.avatar_url}
                        size="sm"
                        class="flex-shrink-0"
                      />
                    <% true -> %>
                      <.human_avatar
                        name={suggestion.name}
                        avatar_url={suggestion.avatar_url}
                        seed={suggestion.avatar_seed}
                        size="sm"
                        class="flex-shrink-0"
                      />
                  <% end %>
                  <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate">
                    <span class="font-medium">{suggestion.name}</span>
                    <span
                      :if={suggestion.participant_type == "broadcast"}
                      class="block text-xs text-base-content/60 truncate"
                    >
                      Notify everyone in the channel
                    </span>
                  </span>
                  <span class={[
                    "rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider",
                    suggestion.participant_type == "broadcast" && "bg-warning/10 text-warning",
                    suggestion.participant_type == "agent" && "bg-primary/10 text-primary",
                    suggestion.participant_type == "user" && "bg-base-300 text-base-content/50"
                  ]}>
                    {suggestion.participant_type}
                  </span>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%!-- Pill-shaped compose bar --%>
          <div class="compose-pill-bar">
            <button
              type="button"
              id="compose-attach-button"
              phx-hook="UploadButton"
              phx-click="upload_dialog_open"
              class="compose-pill-attach cursor-pointer text-base-content/50 hover:bg-base-300/50 transition-colors"
              title="Attach files"
            >
              <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
            </button>

            <textarea
              name="compose[text]"
              id={@compose_form[:text].id}
              data-draft-key={if @active_space, do: "chat-draft:" <> @active_space.id, else: nil}
              placeholder={"Message ##{masked_space_name(assigns, (@active_space && @active_space.name) || "")}"}
              autocomplete="off"
              rows="1"
              class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm resize-none"
              style="line-height:1.5;padding:4px 0;min-height:28px;max-height:200px;overflow-y:auto;field-sizing:content"
              phx-hook="ComposeInput"
            >{Phoenix.HTML.Form.normalize_value("text", @compose_form[:text].value)}</textarea>

            <button
              type="submit"
              class="compose-pill-send"
              disabled={is_nil(@current_participant) or composer_empty?(@compose_form)}
              aria-label="Send message"
              title="Send"
            >
              <span class="hero-paper-airplane size-4 -rotate-45"></span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p
            :for={error <- upload_errors(@uploads.attachments)}
            class="text-xs text-error"
          >
            {upload_error_to_string(error)}
          </p>

          <div :for={entry <- @uploads.attachments.entries}>
            <p
              :for={error <- upload_errors(@uploads.attachments, entry)}
              class="text-xs text-error"
            >
              {entry.client_name}: {upload_error_to_string(error)}
            </p>
          </div>
        </.form>

        <%!-- Always-present upload submission form. Lives OUTSIDE #compose-form
             (HTML forbids nested forms) so the modal's Send button + textarea
             can target it via the HTML5 `form="upload-send-form"` attribute.
             The form is rendered unconditionally so:
               (a) `inputEl.form` resolves on first paste (no chicken-and-egg
                   with `:if={entries != []}` form-rendering).
               (b) LiveView's `pushInput` → `pushFormSubmit` always finds the
                   form to serialize when the user submits.
             The hidden file input (`live_file_input`) is the form's only
             direct child; visible UI for caption + Send lives inside the
             modal panel and links back to this form via `form=...`. --%>
        <form
          :if={@active_space && is_nil(@active_space.archived_at)}
          id="upload-send-form"
          phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
          phx-submit="upload_send"
          phx-change="upload_caption_change"
          class="hidden"
        >
          <.live_file_input upload={@uploads.attachments} class="sr-only" />
        </form>

        <p :if={is_nil(@current_participant) && @active_space} class="mt-1 text-xs text-error">
          Unable to join space — messages are read-only.
        </p>
      </div>

      <.upload_dialog
        open={@upload_dialog_open}
        active_space={@active_space}
        uploads={@uploads}
        caption={@upload_caption}
        tagged_agents={@upload_tagged_agents}
      />
    </div>

    <.canvas_overlay
      canvas={@active_canvas}
      show_versions_panel={@show_versions_panel}
      canvas_versions={@canvas_versions}
      restore_confirm_revision={@restore_confirm_revision}
    />

    <%!-- Embedded surfaces (e.g. inside MeetingLive) leave the meeting
         mini-bar to the parent — the parent already owns the live
         meeting state. Skip the panel here to avoid a double mini-bar. --%>
    <.meeting_panel
      :if={!@embedded}
      in_meeting={@in_meeting}
      active_space={@active_space}
      mic_enabled={@mic_enabled}
      camera_enabled={@camera_enabled}
      screen_share_enabled={@screen_share_enabled}
      meeting_participants={@meeting_participants}
    />
  </div>
</div>

<%!-- Standalone-only modals: settings, new-channel, new-conversation.
     The embedded surface (e.g. meeting chat panel) scopes to one space
     and has no affordances to open these, so the components are skipped
     to keep the embed lean. --%>
<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded}
  module={SettingsComponent}
  id="chat-settings"
  open={@show_settings}
  space={@active_space}
  current_user_id={@user_id}
/>

<%!-- New-channel creation is internal-only chrome — external users never see a
     new-channel affordance, so the modal is also gated off their surface. --%>
<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded and !@external?}
  module={NewChannelComponent}
  id="chat-new-channel"
  open={@show_new_channel_modal}
  org_options={@new_channel_org_options}
  active_org_id={@active_org_id}
/>

<%!-- rbac-external-users M5 stage 3: the DM picker IS available to external
     users, but filtered to allowlisted-org humans (no agents). Thread the
     render-branch flag + acting user so the component can apply
     `Chat.external_dm_permitted?/3` at picker-build time. --%>
<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded}
  module={NewConversationComponent}
  id="chat-new-conversation"
  open={@show_new_conversation_modal}
  user_id={@user_id}
  external?={@external?}
/>

<%!-- Mobile drawer row-actions sheet (task 019fe998). Pin / unpin / hide for
     one drawer conversation row, opened by that row's overflow control.

     Rendered HERE, at the template root, and NOT inside
     `#mobile-channel-browser`: `.sheet` is `position: fixed`, and a CSS
     `transform` on any ancestor becomes the containing block for fixed
     descendants, which centres the panel on the rail instead of the
     viewport. Same reason the guest-invite sheet sits at its LiveView's root.

     Gated to the internal, non-embedded surface, matching the drawer it
     serves. Always rendered (not `:if`-gated on the target) so the panel can
     transition in — `.sheet` is `visibility: hidden` until `.sheet-open`, and
     an element inserted already-open has no starting frame to animate from.
     `row_actions_target/5` returns nil while closed, which keeps the header
     empty rather than holding the last-opened conversation's name. --%>
<.row_actions_sheet
  :if={!@embedded and !@external?}
  target={
    row_actions_target(
      @row_actions_space_id,
      @channels,
      @dm_conversations,
      @pinned_space_ids,
      @user_id
    )
  }
/>

<%!-- Desktop rail row-actions menu (task 019ff8ba stage 1). Same assign, same
     open/close events and same resolver as the sheet above; only the chrome
     and the breakpoint differ. Rendered HERE, at the template root, for the
     reason `move_to_org_dialog/1` is: `#chat-section-list` is
     `overflow-y-auto`, so `overflow-x` computes to `auto` and clips anything
     anchored to a row on both axes.

     The resolver is called a second time rather than bound to a variable
     shared with the sheet: `:if` short-circuits attribute evaluation, and
     these assigns are absent on the embedded and external surfaces. The
     duplicate costs one `list_participants/1` per render, and only while a
     DM's menu is open.

     A DIFFERENT resolver from the sheet's, and deliberately so. The rail's
     Pinned block carries task rows and they now carry a trigger too (Marlowe,
     2026-08-13), so this one also looks in `@pinned_task_spaces`. The sheet
     keeps the conversation-only resolver: the phone drawer's task rows unpin
     on the row itself and never open it, and the sheet's two actions
     (`toggle_pinned`, `hide_channel`) are the wrong verbs for a task pin. --%>
<.row_actions_dialog
  :if={!@embedded and !@external?}
  fabrikam_admin?={@fabrikam_admin?}
  target={
    rail_row_actions_target(
      @row_actions_space_id,
      @channels,
      @dm_conversations,
      @pinned_task_spaces,
      @pinned_space_ids,
      @user_id
    )
  }
/>

<%!--
  Reaction picker — bottom sheet on mobile, centered modal on desktop.
  Shape is controlled by the `reaction-picker` CSS class: below the
  640px breakpoint the panel slides up from the bottom with safe-area
  padding (matches iOS/Android conventions); above it centers as a
  modal card. Escape key closes via phx-window-keydown so keyboard
  users have parity with backdrop click.
--%>
<div
  :if={@reaction_picker_for}
  id="reaction-picker"
  class="reaction-picker fixed inset-0 z-50"
  phx-window-keydown="close_reaction_picker"
  phx-key="Escape"
>
  <div
    class="reaction-picker-scrim absolute inset-0 bg-base-content/20"
    phx-click="close_reaction_picker"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>
  <%!--
    `role="dialog"` without `aria-modal="true"` is an intentional
    downgrade: we don't yet have a focus trap or return-focus-on-close,
    so claiming modality to assistive tech would be a false promise.
    Full focus management lands in PR B (search + a11y feature pass).
  --%>
  <div
    class="reaction-picker-panel rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-3 shadow-xl"
    role="dialog"
    aria-label="Add reaction"
  >
    <div class="mb-2 flex items-center justify-between">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/60">
        Add reaction
      </span>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="close_reaction_picker"
        title="Close"
        aria-label="Close reaction picker"
        class="reaction-picker-close rounded p-1 text-base-content/50 hover:bg-base-200 hover:text-base-content"
      >
        <span class="hero-x-mark size-5"></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="reaction-picker-grid">
      <button
        :for={emoji <- @reaction_picker_emojis}
        type="button"
        phx-click="react"
        phx-value-message-id={@reaction_picker_for}
        phx-value-emoji={emoji}
        title={"React with #{emoji}"}
        aria-label={"React with #{emoji}"}
        class="reaction-picker-tile rounded hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors"
      >
        {emoji}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%!--
  Quick-react popover (mobile). Triggered by double-tap on a message
  authored by someone else — see the `LongpressMenu` JS hook, which
  despite the legacy name now listens for a double-tap gesture rather
  than a 450ms hold. Scrim + blur fade in, target message clones and
  animates to viewport center via `MessageLift`, and the emoji pill
  floats above the lifted clone. Pill position is driven by
  `--clone-half-h`, set by the hook at mount. The historical action
  card (Copy / Open in thread / Pin) was removed: Copy duplicated the
  browser's native selection menu on mobile, and Pin was frequently
  triggered by accident. Thread-open is deferred to a follow-up UX
  pass; desktop still exposes both via the hover action bar.
--%>
<div
  :if={@longpress_menu_for}
  id="longpress-menu"
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50"
  role="dialog"
  aria-label="Message actions"
  data-target-message-id={@longpress_menu_for}
  phx-hook="MessageLift"
>
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0 longpress-scrim"
    phx-click="close_longpress_menu"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <%!-- Emoji quick-react pill, floats above the lifted clone.
       Each tap fires `react` (persists the reaction via Chat.toggle_reaction
       → close_picker/1 closes both reaction_picker_for and longpress_menu_for). --%>
  <div class="longpress-pill" role="group" aria-label="Quick reactions">
    <button
      :for={emoji <- ~w(👍 🎉 ✅ ❤️ 😂 🙏)}
      type="button"
      class="longpress-pill-btn"
      title={"React with #{emoji}"}
      phx-click="react"
      phx-value-message-id={@longpress_menu_for}
      phx-value-emoji={emoji}
    >
      {emoji}
    </button>
    <div class="longpress-pill-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="longpress-pill-btn longpress-pill-more"
      title="More emoji"
      aria-label="More emoji"
      phx-click={
        JS.push("open_reaction_picker", value: %{"message-id" => @longpress_menu_for})
        |> JS.push("close_longpress_menu")
      }
    >
      <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>

<.image_lightbox url={@lightbox_url} />

<%!-- Per-message actions sheet (task 019e0f29 Stage 3 — fixes Marlowe's bug
     report that the chat-message 3-dot dropdown didn't open on touch).
     Single Sheet at the page bottom, sourced by :open_message_actions_id;
     same pattern as the per-row task-actions sheet from Task 05 Stage 2.

     Actions are the chat-message hover-toolbar's text-able actions
     (Copy / Pin / Reply). Quick-emoji react row + reaction picker are
     deferred — they'd need their own design beyond a simple action list.
     The Edit item lands in Stage 4 once the editable-messages contract
     ships. --%>
<%!-- Listener for scroll-to-message events from the correction header
     (task 019e0f29 Stage 6, contract Section D.4). Hidden div; the
     ChatScrollToMessage hook drives smooth scroll + brief pulse. --%>
<div id="chat-scroll-to-message-listener" phx-hook="ChatScrollToMessage" class="hidden"></div>

<%!-- Version history popover (task 019e0f29 Stage 6, contract Section D.2).
     Surfaces when @version_history is set (clicking the `(edited)` affix on
     a message bubble). --%>
<PlatformWeb.Components.ChatVersionHistory.chat_version_history
  open={@version_history != nil}
  versions={(@version_history && @version_history.versions) || []}
/>

<%!-- Removal-warning modal (task 019e0f29 Stage 5, contract Section F.4
     Policy 4). Surfaces only when the user's edit shortens / removes
     content. Copy locked in by Marlowe on 2026-05-11 review round 1:
     terse, factual, no editorial. Buttons: Cancel (keeps editor open
     with the user's draft) / Edit anyway (fires the actual edit). --%>
<div
  :if={@pending_save_edit}
  id="edit-removal-warning"
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/60 backdrop-blur-sm"
  phx-window-keydown="cancel_save_edit"
  phx-key="escape"
>
  <div
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="edit-removal-warning-title"
    class="w-full max-w-md rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-5 shadow-xl"
  >
    <h2 id="edit-removal-warning-title" class="text-base font-semibold text-base-content">
      Edit removes text.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
      Agents that already read this still have the original in their memory.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="cancel_save_edit"
        class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        Cancel
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="confirm_save_edit"
        class="rounded-md bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-primary-content hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        Edit anyway
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<.sheet
  :if={@open_message_actions_id}
  id="message-actions-sheet"
  open={true}
  placement={:bottom}
  on_close="close_message_actions"
>
  <:title>Message actions</:title>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
    <%!-- Quick-reaction strip (task 01a000c0 stage 1).

         WHY A STRIP AND NOT AN "Add reaction…" MENU ROW: design canvas
         01a000c4-5bd3-795c-b982-acbb9488e5f8 (ADR-0046) cut the menu row.
         On touch there is no hover, so the always-visible dashed "+" is
         today the only add-reaction path on a phone — a single tap. A menu
         row would turn that one tap into four (double-tap, read the menu,
         tap the row, wait for the picker, tap an emoji). One tap here has
         to stay one tap.

         EMOJI SET: @quick_emojis, the same assign the desktop hover action
         row renders (chat_message.ex ~line 159), so pointer and touch
         cannot drift. Do not hardcode a literal list here; if the set is
         wrong, change the assign in chat_live.ex.

         THE "+" IS IN THIS ROW, NOT A ROW OF ITS OWN: Harper's ruling —
         "the reaction should be next to the other emojis as a + sign; when
         you hit that you get the other options". Stage 3 moves the desktop
         "+" into the hover action row, which already renders these same
         four @quick_emojis, so touch and pointer end up the same shape and
         the same gesture. A labelled "More reactions…" menu row on one
         surface and a glyph on the other would be two ways to do one thing.
         The "+" is an additional CONTROL, not a fifth entry in the assign.

         SIZING: 44x44 hit targets (size-11), the vertical hairline before
         the "+", and the "+"'s own base-200 fill / scale-on-press are
         borrowed from the orphaned .longpress-pill, .longpress-pill-divider
         and .longpress-pill-more treatment in app.css rather than
         reinvented. --%>
    <div
      id="message-actions-quick-reactions"
      class="flex items-center gap-1 px-1 pb-2"
      role="group"
      aria-label="Quick reactions"
    >
      <button
        :for={emoji <- @quick_emojis}
        type="button"
        aria-label={"React with #{emoji}"}
        title={"React with #{emoji}"}
        phx-click={
          Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("react")
          |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
        }
        phx-value-message-id={@open_message_actions_id}
        phx-value-emoji={emoji}
        class="flex size-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-2xl leading-none text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 active:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        {emoji}
      </button>
      <%!-- Hairline before the "+", matching .longpress-pill-divider (1px x
           24px on --color-base-300). It says the "+" is a different KIND of
           target from the four beside it — one opens the picker, the others
           react — without pulling it out of the row. --%>
      <div class="h-6 w-px shrink-0 bg-base-300" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <%!-- Escape hatch for anything outside @quick_emojis. Same event chain
           the deleted "More reactions…" row used: open the existing
           #reaction-picker, then close this sheet. Filled on --color-base-200
           with a press-scale rather than a press-fill (borrowed verbatim from
           .longpress-pill-more / .longpress-pill-btn:active), because at rest
           it already carries that fill. No --color-primary: an add-reaction
           control is not an action to advertise. --%>
      <button
        type="button"
        id="message-actions-more-reactions"
        aria-label="More reactions"
        title="More reactions"
        phx-click={
          Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("open_reaction_picker",
            value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id}
          )
          |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
        }
        class="flex size-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-base-200 text-base-content transition-transform active:scale-90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="border-t border-base-300" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("toggle_inline_thread",
          value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id}
        )
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Reply in thread</span>
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("pin_toggle", value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id})
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-bookmark size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Pin / Unpin</span>
    </button>
    <%!-- Edit affordance — Policy 3 of the editable-messages contract
         (own non-agent text messages only). The message struct is lifted
         into @open_message_actions_msg by the open_message_actions
         handler so the visibility filter can be evaluated at template
         render time. The hover-pencil affordance on the chat row was
         removed in task 019e2452; this sheet item is now the SOLE edit
         entry point on all viewports. --%>
    <button
      :if={
        @open_message_actions_msg && @current_participant &&
          @open_message_actions_msg.participant_id == @current_participant.id &&
          @open_message_actions_msg.content_type == "text"
      }
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("edit_message_clicked",
          value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id}
        )
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-pencil-square size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Edit message</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</.sheet>

<%!-- Schedule-deletion confirm dialog (task 019f4eaa stage 6). Archive is
     instant + reversible with no modal; only this destructive step confirms. --%>
<.schedule_delete_modal
  resource={@delete_modal}
  retention_days={Platform.Tenancy.Lifecycle.retention_days()}
/>

<%!-- "Move to organisation…" confirmation (task 019fd76a stage 1). Rendered
     ONCE for the surface, as a top-level sibling: a dialog nested inside the
     rail's scrolling `<nav>` would be clipped by its `overflow-y-auto`. The
     confirm handler reads its ids from `@reassign_confirm` on the server, so
     this markup carries no channel or destination id of its own. --%>
<.move_to_org_picker picker={@reassign_picker} />
<.move_to_org_dialog confirm={@reassign_confirm} />

<%!-- Archive undo toast (task 019f4eaa). Archive is instant + dialog-free by
     design; this says what it took and keeps the reversal one click away.
     Top-level sibling — pinned chrome must never nest in an :if region. --%>
<.archive_undo_toast undo={@undo_archive} />

<%!-- Junk-batch confirmation modal (M5b/019f6e2c stage 4). Opened by
     `PlatformWeb.ChatLive.CanvasHooks` when a `junk_batch:*` canvas
     action_row is clicked; closed by `close_junk_batch_modal` or the
     backdrop. Shape mirrors the tasks-live `#reopen-modal` (mobile-first
     bottom-sheet, centered dialog on sm+). Empty-batch guard: when
     `preview_count == 0`, the destructive button is hidden entirely
     and only Close remains — that IS the acceptance-criterion-5
     empty-state affordance. --%>
<div
  :if={@show_junk_batch_modal && @junk_batch_target}
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-end sm:items-center justify-center"
  id="junk-batch-modal"
  data-role="junk-batch-modal"
>
  <%!-- Backdrop --%>
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40" phx-click="close_junk_batch_modal" />

  <%!-- Sheet / dialog --%>
  <div class="relative w-full max-w-lg rounded-t-2xl sm:rounded-2xl bg-base-100 shadow-2xl pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)] max-h-[90vh] overflow-y-auto">
    <%!-- Header --%>
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-base-300 px-4 py-3">
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold">Roll back this batch</h2>
        <p class="mt-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/60">
          Meeting-triage rollback
        </p>
      </div>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="close_junk_batch_modal"
        class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost btn-square"
        aria-label="Close"
      >
        <span class="hero-x-mark size-4"></span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <%!-- Body --%>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 px-4 py-4">
      <%= if @junk_batch_target.preview_count > 0 do %>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80">
          This will soft-delete
          <span class="font-semibold" data-role="junk-batch-preview-count">
            {@junk_batch_target.preview_count}
          </span>
          {if @junk_batch_target.preview_count == 1, do: "task", else: "tasks"} filed from this canvas. Continue?
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80" data-role="junk-batch-empty-note">
          Nothing to roll back — every task from this batch has already been handled.
        </p>
      <% end %>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 pt-1">
        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="close_junk_batch_modal"
          class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm"
        >
          Close
        </button>
        <button
          :if={@junk_batch_target.preview_count > 0}
          type="button"
          phx-click="confirm_junk_batch"
          class="btn btn-error btn-sm"
          data-role="junk-batch-confirm"
        >
          Junk {@junk_batch_target.preview_count} {if @junk_batch_target.preview_count == 1,
            do: "task",
            else: "tasks"}
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
